1
00:00:00,678 --> 00:00:02,679
(Kim Yeon Koung, the volleyball queen,)

2
00:00:02,987 --> 00:00:05,589
(has become a rookie coach.)

3
00:00:05,946 --> 00:00:08,285
(Fourteen players she handpicked herself)

4
00:00:08,514 --> 00:00:10,081
The launch ceremony...What's going on?

5
00:00:11,084 --> 00:00:12,017
What's going on?

6
00:00:12,252 --> 00:00:13,953
(For various reasons,)

7
00:00:14,354 --> 00:00:16,422
(these players
couldn't join the pro league.)

8
00:00:16,557 --> 00:00:19,559
(Fourteen different stories...)

9
00:00:19,559 --> 00:00:22,094
(of fourteen underdogs)

10
00:00:22,294 --> 00:00:25,196
Our ultimate goal is to make
the eighth pro team.

11
00:00:25,532 --> 00:00:28,601
We're going to play against seven teams.

12
00:00:29,102 --> 00:00:31,036
(If they can't win
the majority of matches,)

13
00:00:31,038 --> 00:00:33,406
(the team will be disbanded.)

14
00:00:33,407 --> 00:00:35,174
(Their first opponent is...)

15
00:00:35,542 --> 00:00:37,510
(the high school champion,
Geunyoung Girls' High.)

16
00:00:40,681 --> 00:00:42,148
(Fiery rookies versus...)

17
00:00:42,149 --> 00:00:44,083
(older players carrying their own scars)

18
00:00:45,686 --> 00:00:46,719
Set one starts.

19
00:00:48,855 --> 00:00:49,688
Hey!

20
00:00:54,298 --> 00:00:56,559
(Facing a crisis in the first set)

21
00:00:57,093 --> 00:01:00,762
(The rookie coach in deep trouble...)

22
00:01:01,010 --> 00:01:03,940
(calls for the tactic of the legend.)

23
00:01:06,177 --> 00:01:09,212
(The tactic by the rookie coach...)

24
00:01:09,213 --> 00:01:11,381
(paid off.)

25
00:01:11,916 --> 00:01:14,518
(Her other tactic was blocking.)

26
00:01:15,486 --> 00:01:18,421
(And it was also a success.)

27
00:01:18,589 --> 00:01:21,925
(Tactical volleyball
you've never seen before)

28
00:01:22,093 --> 00:01:24,995
(Blocking masters, Wonder Dogs)

29
00:01:25,563 --> 00:01:28,698
(They single-handedly
caught up in set one.)

30
00:01:29,734 --> 00:01:32,402
(Second set, Geunyoung Girls' High 12
: Wonder Dogs 16)

31
00:01:33,037 --> 00:01:34,938
The gap is down to four points.

32
00:01:34,939 --> 00:01:36,339
It's 16 to 12 now.

33
00:01:36,941 --> 00:01:39,910
(At this rate,
they could win the second set too.)

34
00:01:40,578 --> 00:01:42,112
- Nice serve!
- Nice serve!

35
00:01:43,147 --> 00:01:44,247
Myoung-Hwa's serve.

36
00:01:45,449 --> 00:01:47,016
- I got it!
- Go to the front!

37
00:01:47,017 --> 00:01:48,384
- Go!
- Get it!

38
00:01:48,385 --> 00:01:51,020
(Da Eun's spike)

39
00:01:51,021 --> 00:01:52,388
- Nice, Da Eun!
- Let's go!

40
00:01:52,757 --> 00:01:55,225
- Spike from the middle!
- Yes.

41
00:01:55,360 --> 00:01:57,026
It fired straight through.

42
00:01:58,929 --> 00:02:00,263
It was a touchout!

43
00:02:01,298 --> 00:02:03,566
Geunyoung Girls' High's usual plays...

44
00:02:03,567 --> 00:02:07,236
kept getting blocked from the wing.

45
00:02:08,239 --> 00:02:11,374
So they're changing their attack points...

46
00:02:11,375 --> 00:02:13,710
- to the center for a change.
- That's right.

47
00:02:15,946 --> 00:02:16,913
Serve!

48
00:02:17,948 --> 00:02:20,283
It's Eun Chae's serve
from Geunyoung Girls' High.

49
00:02:20,284 --> 00:02:21,217
Let's go!

50
00:02:21,719 --> 00:02:23,319
Nice pass.

51
00:02:24,155 --> 00:02:25,255
A spike!

52
00:02:25,790 --> 00:02:27,190
That was good defense.

53
00:02:27,191 --> 00:02:29,092
- Go!
- Pass it!

54
00:02:29,093 --> 00:02:30,527
They sent it over for now.

55
00:02:30,527 --> 00:02:31,660
Come on, Young In!

56
00:02:32,296 --> 00:02:33,596
- Come on, Young In!
- Hey!

57
00:02:34,465 --> 00:02:35,498
Come on, Young In!

58
00:02:35,499 --> 00:02:37,633
That's a shaky connection.

59
00:02:37,635 --> 00:02:39,069
(A setting error)

60
00:02:40,604 --> 00:02:42,471
(Geunyoung Girls' High
bringing up their energy)

61
00:02:42,873 --> 00:02:44,373
(Geunyoung Girls' High 14
: Wonder Dogs 11)

62
00:02:45,042 --> 00:02:47,176
Sorry, my bad.

63
00:02:48,178 --> 00:02:50,246
(Na-Yeon's tosses are
starting to get shaky.)

64
00:02:50,614 --> 00:02:53,950
(They need a plan to turn the tide.)

65
00:02:54,018 --> 00:02:56,219
Double substitution.

66
00:02:57,221 --> 00:03:00,957
- Wonder Dogs are making...
- A double substitution.

67
00:03:00,958 --> 00:03:03,159
- We can do this!
- Let's go for this!

68
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:07,530
Sol and Tamira have come in now.

69
00:03:07,531 --> 00:03:08,698
(Young In out, Tamira in)

70
00:03:09,633 --> 00:03:10,766
- Let's get it!
- Let's go!

71
00:03:10,768 --> 00:03:12,302
(A change in their attacking strategy)

72
00:03:12,970 --> 00:03:14,704
Sol is serving now.

73
00:03:17,341 --> 00:03:18,241
My ball.
I got it.

74
00:03:20,044 --> 00:03:21,277
Pass it over!

75
00:03:21,278 --> 00:03:22,545
(Soo Min's spike)

76
00:03:22,546 --> 00:03:23,613
Open spike!

77
00:03:23,614 --> 00:03:24,681
Over there!

78
00:03:25,115 --> 00:03:26,849
They're going after it, and they saved it!

79
00:03:26,850 --> 00:03:27,917
My ball.

80
00:03:28,652 --> 00:03:30,119
Free ball for Geunyoung Girls' High.

81
00:03:30,120 --> 00:03:31,287
- Go!
- Up high!

82
00:03:31,288 --> 00:03:32,789
(Another strong spike)

83
00:03:32,957 --> 00:03:33,990
A strong spike!

84
00:03:34,425 --> 00:03:35,291
Don't lose it!

85
00:03:36,594 --> 00:03:38,128
Wait, I got it!

86
00:03:39,230 --> 00:03:40,163
A back set.

87
00:03:40,164 --> 00:03:42,098
(Da Eun's spike)

88
00:03:42,266 --> 00:03:43,533
Nice!

89
00:03:45,469 --> 00:03:47,336
Off the block and down.

90
00:03:47,338 --> 00:03:49,272
- Nice flow!
- You're doing great, girls.

91
00:03:49,273 --> 00:03:51,241
The offense is picking up.

92
00:03:51,241 --> 00:03:52,041
Yes, coach.

93
00:03:52,476 --> 00:03:54,477
The gap is now two points. 17 to 15.

94
00:03:54,511 --> 00:03:55,578
Serve.

95
00:03:58,716 --> 00:03:59,949
That was a nice pass.

96
00:04:00,384 --> 00:04:01,217
It's a free ball.

97
00:04:02,953 --> 00:04:05,121
- Set's up. Oh, that was shaky.
- It was shaky.

98
00:04:06,223 --> 00:04:07,156
Get it!

99
00:04:07,157 --> 00:04:08,524
- I'll pass.
- Coming!

100
00:04:08,525 --> 00:04:09,625
That's it! Cover!

101
00:04:09,727 --> 00:04:11,728
Free ball for Geunyoung Girls' High again.

102
00:04:11,795 --> 00:04:13,329
Yes!

103
00:04:14,031 --> 00:04:17,300
Another strong strike! Nice one!

104
00:04:17,301 --> 00:04:18,301
(Another point by Soo Min)

105
00:04:18,302 --> 00:04:19,602
Nice going, Soo Min!

106
00:04:20,237 --> 00:04:21,637
(The principal feeling proud)

107
00:04:21,638 --> 00:04:23,205
Let's go!

108
00:04:23,674 --> 00:04:25,708
Only a one-point difference now.

109
00:04:25,709 --> 00:04:26,842
It's 18 to 17.

110
00:04:27,278 --> 00:04:28,545
- Get out of the way!
- I got it!

111
00:04:28,545 --> 00:04:29,845
- Watch it.
- Hit it!

112
00:04:30,848 --> 00:04:31,915
Spike!

113
00:04:33,050 --> 00:04:34,951
(Soo Min scores again.)

114
00:04:35,185 --> 00:04:36,919
They've finally caught up!

115
00:04:37,554 --> 00:04:38,921
(Wonder Dogs try to come back.)

116
00:04:38,922 --> 00:04:40,256
A powerful strike from the right.

117
00:04:40,891 --> 00:04:41,958
They kept it alive!

118
00:04:41,959 --> 00:04:43,560
A change to turn the game around.

119
00:04:46,730 --> 00:04:47,697
Geunyoung Girls' High spikes!

120
00:04:48,332 --> 00:04:51,034
(Off the block and out)

121
00:04:52,303 --> 00:04:55,005
Geunyoung Girls' High pulled off
the comeback!

122
00:04:55,973 --> 00:04:58,374
- We're doing great!
- Great work!

123
00:05:00,277 --> 00:05:01,410
Keep up the momentum!

124
00:05:02,479 --> 00:05:04,474
(The atmosphere...)

125
00:05:04,474 --> 00:05:06,081
(is getting tense.)

126
00:05:06,383 --> 00:05:09,552
(Second set, Geunyoung Girls' High 19
: Wonder Dogs 18)

127
00:05:10,421 --> 00:05:12,021
(And the next serve is...)

128
00:05:12,022 --> 00:05:14,123
- Nice serve, Kim Soo Min!
- Nice serve, Kim Soo Min!

129
00:05:15,159 --> 00:05:16,626
Watch out for a short serve.

130
00:05:16,627 --> 00:05:17,894
(Here comes a short serve.)

131
00:05:26,804 --> 00:05:29,005
It hits the net and drops.

132
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:33,142
(The momentum has completely shifted
to Geunyoung Girls' High.)

133
00:05:34,578 --> 00:05:37,614
(Second set, Geunyoung Girls' High 21
: Wonder Dogs 18)

134
00:05:40,484 --> 00:05:41,884
Let's keep this going!

135
00:05:42,653 --> 00:05:44,787
I didn't know what to do.

136
00:05:46,724 --> 00:05:49,959
I think my substitution choice...

137
00:05:50,042 --> 00:05:52,328
cost us the momentum.

138
00:05:52,329 --> 00:05:54,130
But in my mind,

139
00:05:54,391 --> 00:05:57,093
I knew it was a tough situation,

140
00:05:57,501 --> 00:05:59,735
but I wanted to have faith in them.

141
00:05:59,903 --> 00:06:03,539
I was hoping they could
overcome it on their own.

142
00:06:06,110 --> 00:06:07,644
Her serve hit the net.

143
00:06:07,644 --> 00:06:09,645
(A serve error)

144
00:06:10,214 --> 00:06:13,383
- She tries to pass it, but fails!
- Yeah.

145
00:06:15,753 --> 00:06:16,853
A standing spike!

146
00:06:17,521 --> 00:06:18,621
It touched the net!

147
00:06:18,622 --> 00:06:20,923
(Net violation)

148
00:06:20,958 --> 00:06:22,992
That's a net violation.

149
00:06:23,460 --> 00:06:25,227
It's 24 to 20.

150
00:06:25,229 --> 00:06:27,564
Geunyoung Girls' High is at a set point
in the second set.

151
00:06:28,365 --> 00:06:29,565
Let's go!

152
00:06:29,733 --> 00:06:32,101
- We can do this!
- Don't lose this one!

153
00:06:33,070 --> 00:06:34,504
Look out for the middle.

154
00:06:34,505 --> 00:06:37,240
- Watch it coming.
- Watch the middle part.

155
00:06:38,542 --> 00:06:40,676
(Ye Bin's serve)

156
00:06:42,279 --> 00:06:43,746
- Mine!
- Pass it!

157
00:06:44,314 --> 00:06:45,514
(A shaky pass)

158
00:06:48,752 --> 00:06:51,787
- It was way too low.
- Too low.

159
00:06:56,093 --> 00:07:00,329
Geunyoung Girls' High
wins the second set, 25 to 20.

160
00:07:00,564 --> 00:07:02,331
This could actually make...

161
00:07:02,332 --> 00:07:04,633
Wonder Dogs players lose
a bit of confidence,

162
00:07:04,635 --> 00:07:07,270
since Geunyoung Girls' High is playing
with a lot more confidence now.

163
00:07:07,271 --> 00:07:09,706
- We could've done better.
- No, you did great.

164
00:07:09,706 --> 00:07:10,739
- Yes!
- You did great.

165
00:07:10,741 --> 00:07:12,775
Your defense looks good right now.

166
00:07:12,776 --> 00:07:14,043
Your blocking is solid.

167
00:07:15,512 --> 00:07:17,980
(However, on the other side...)

168
00:07:20,551 --> 00:07:21,451
Listen, guys.

169
00:07:24,521 --> 00:07:26,755
When you attack, remember this.

170
00:07:26,757 --> 00:07:29,092
Their defense is all in the back.

171
00:07:29,426 --> 00:07:30,760
They're all in the back.

172
00:07:31,361 --> 00:07:32,761
I was watching the game,

173
00:07:32,896 --> 00:07:37,500
and I realized that
the opponent's defenders were pulled back.

174
00:07:37,501 --> 00:07:42,638
So I thought we could try
using the tip play.

175
00:07:42,639 --> 00:07:45,141
You could think of it
as tricking the opponent.

176
00:07:45,142 --> 00:07:47,377
It's not just a strong spike,

177
00:07:47,377 --> 00:07:49,678
but hitting the ball into a void spot.

178
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:52,248
We call this a feint, a tip.

179
00:07:52,716 --> 00:07:54,083
Like I said, they're all in the back.

180
00:07:54,518 --> 00:07:56,385
- If you're going to tip, aim over here.
- Yes, coach.

181
00:07:56,386 --> 00:07:57,686
- In zone three.
- Okay.

182
00:07:57,688 --> 00:07:59,622
This zone is totally open.

183
00:07:59,623 --> 00:08:00,857
- Got it?
- Yes, coach.

184
00:08:01,492 --> 00:08:03,927
- We can still do this.
- Thank you, coach.

185
00:08:03,927 --> 00:08:04,994
- Let's go!
- Let's do this!

186
00:08:04,995 --> 00:08:06,495
- One, two, three. Let's go!
- Let's go!

187
00:08:06,496 --> 00:08:07,329
Go get them!

188
00:08:07,965 --> 00:08:09,499
It's clear to both teams now.

189
00:08:09,499 --> 00:08:12,267
- They need to take this third set to win.
- Of course.

190
00:08:13,270 --> 00:08:17,673
Geunyoung Girls' High
won the second set, 25 to 20.

191
00:08:17,674 --> 00:08:20,576
Since they were overtaken
late in the last set,

192
00:08:20,577 --> 00:08:23,145
- Wonder Dogs need a strong start now.
- Yes, that's correct.

193
00:08:24,114 --> 00:08:25,448
Let's go with the same players.

194
00:08:26,350 --> 00:08:29,152
- Watch out for a short serve.
- A short serve is coming.

195
00:08:29,286 --> 00:08:31,020
- Get ready.
- Yes.

196
00:08:31,021 --> 00:08:33,055
Go get them!

197
00:08:36,927 --> 00:08:40,396
(Set three begins under heavy tension)

198
00:08:40,664 --> 00:08:41,731
The third set starts.

199
00:08:42,432 --> 00:08:43,632
- Nice serve.
- Hit it!

200
00:08:44,568 --> 00:08:46,235
Watch the ball! Go!

201
00:08:48,238 --> 00:08:49,438
(The ball touched the ground.)

202
00:08:53,744 --> 00:08:54,644
It's in! Yes!

203
00:08:56,580 --> 00:08:58,414
(Third set, Geunyoung Girls' High 0
: Wonder Dogs 1)

204
00:08:58,415 --> 00:09:00,216
- That was a clean play.
- Nice work.

205
00:09:00,217 --> 00:09:02,752
- Keep this momentum!
- Let's lead from the start!

206
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:05,255
Stay focused.
Let's take control from the start.

207
00:09:05,255 --> 00:09:06,922
Wonder Players probably know as well.

208
00:09:06,923 --> 00:09:09,258
- They need to grab it from the start.
- Yes.

209
00:09:09,793 --> 00:09:12,561
(Myoung-Hwa's serve)

210
00:09:14,531 --> 00:09:15,698
Watch the front.

211
00:09:15,699 --> 00:09:16,566
Got it.

212
00:09:17,201 --> 00:09:18,201
Hit it!

213
00:09:18,535 --> 00:09:20,870
(Is it a point for us?)

214
00:09:20,871 --> 00:09:22,305
- Hit it!
- They're passing.

215
00:09:23,874 --> 00:09:24,707
- Yes!
- Nice!

216
00:09:24,708 --> 00:09:26,309
(An incredible dig by Enkhsoyol)

217
00:09:26,310 --> 00:09:27,544
Enkhsoyol's dig.

218
00:09:31,815 --> 00:09:32,848
Pass it!

219
00:09:34,284 --> 00:09:35,484
(They saved it!)

220
00:09:35,485 --> 00:09:36,952
They passed it. A second touch.

221
00:09:36,953 --> 00:09:39,988
We're not ready for a spike.
Watch out for a tip!

222
00:09:39,990 --> 00:09:41,791
Young In, get ready for the set!

223
00:09:42,693 --> 00:09:46,863
(Young In pushes it over in a hurry.)

224
00:09:46,863 --> 00:09:48,430
That was a bit rushed.

225
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:50,432
Get ready!

226
00:09:51,758 --> 00:09:52,867
Here!

227
00:09:54,905 --> 00:09:55,905
You should be ready!

228
00:09:59,799 --> 00:10:01,965
(Chae-Rim failed
to send the ball over the net.)

229
00:10:01,965 --> 00:10:03,169
She pushed it over.

230
00:10:03,985 --> 00:10:05,515
Okay!

231
00:10:05,516 --> 00:10:07,406
(We also earned a point.)

232
00:10:08,051 --> 00:10:09,488
Young In, why didn't you prepare
in advance?

233
00:10:09,507 --> 00:10:11,810
- You hit only once. Get ready.
- Okay.

234
00:10:11,887 --> 00:10:14,481
A fierce start between Wonder Dogs
and Geunyoung Girls' High.

235
00:10:14,849 --> 00:10:17,716
Knowing how crucial
the start of the third set is,

236
00:10:17,723 --> 00:10:20,462
- right.
- both teams are playing tense.

237
00:10:24,548 --> 00:10:25,858
Jump!

238
00:10:25,958 --> 00:10:27,858
(Led by their ace, Soo Min,)

239
00:10:27,884 --> 00:10:29,629
She charged in and hit hard.

240
00:10:31,406 --> 00:10:35,477
(Geunyoung Girls' High begins their push.)

241
00:10:35,502 --> 00:10:37,100
It hits the net,
but Myoung-Hwa keeps it alive.

242
00:10:37,674 --> 00:10:38,674
Back toss.

243
00:10:38,687 --> 00:10:40,106
Young In, please.

244
00:10:40,530 --> 00:10:42,557
Don't pass it off, and turn it around!

245
00:10:45,378 --> 00:10:47,580
(Young In's attack failed.)

246
00:10:48,547 --> 00:10:51,917
(An exciting block)

247
00:10:54,905 --> 00:10:57,472
Geunyoung Girls' High takes the lead
with a block.

248
00:10:59,534 --> 00:11:01,181
When Young In attacks...

249
00:11:01,414 --> 00:11:03,028
from the right side,

250
00:11:03,347 --> 00:11:04,966
- she prefers hitting straight.
- Okay.

251
00:11:05,831 --> 00:11:07,726
(The seasoned coach's accurate analysis)

252
00:11:07,726 --> 00:11:09,299
The Geunyoung Girls' High players are...

253
00:11:09,606 --> 00:11:12,526
positioning themselves perfectly,

254
00:11:12,527 --> 00:11:14,306
knowing where to be...

255
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:16,434
to defend against Young In.

256
00:11:18,569 --> 00:11:21,872
(The game enters a new phase.)

257
00:11:22,848 --> 00:11:25,184
(The rookie coach is deep in thought.)

258
00:11:25,747 --> 00:11:29,170
Young In, if the ball is bad,

259
00:11:29,483 --> 00:11:30,589
place it at position three.

260
00:11:31,283 --> 00:11:33,809
- Okay.
- Do you get it?

261
00:11:37,069 --> 00:11:40,899
Enkhsoyol, everyone is out in defense.

262
00:11:40,974 --> 00:11:42,607
- So you can tip it to position three.
- Okay.

263
00:11:43,614 --> 00:11:48,073
Coach Kim sees the Wonder Dogs
being chased and overtaken.

264
00:11:52,546 --> 00:11:53,546
Mine!

265
00:11:55,614 --> 00:11:58,016
(Position three is really empty.)

266
00:12:03,211 --> 00:12:06,171
They shouldn't make a mistake here.

267
00:12:06,983 --> 00:12:09,228
(She was instructed to tip the ball,)

268
00:12:10,213 --> 00:12:11,730
Spike!

269
00:12:11,731 --> 00:12:13,032
(but she hit a powerful spike.)

270
00:12:13,966 --> 00:12:16,101
(Oh, that...)

271
00:12:16,953 --> 00:12:19,580
Enkhsoyol,
I told you they'd be out in defense.

272
00:12:19,581 --> 00:12:22,574
- Where did I tell you to place it?
- Position three.

273
00:12:23,854 --> 00:12:26,745
I'm Enkhsoyol, and I'm from Mongolia.

274
00:12:27,760 --> 00:12:31,083
Everyone is out in defense,
so tip it to position three.

275
00:12:31,084 --> 00:12:33,119
(Finally she understood
the instruction now.)

276
00:12:34,986 --> 00:12:36,726
Spike!

277
00:12:36,739 --> 00:12:38,157
I said everyone was out in defense!

278
00:12:38,260 --> 00:12:40,743
Enkhsoyol hits it to the left.

279
00:12:41,129 --> 00:12:42,394
Enkhsoyol!

280
00:12:43,536 --> 00:12:45,264
Tip it to position three!

281
00:12:46,232 --> 00:12:47,382
(Unexpected miscommunication)

282
00:12:47,395 --> 00:12:49,168
I'm really going crazy because of her.

283
00:12:49,985 --> 00:12:52,505
Before the players launch an attack,

284
00:12:52,565 --> 00:12:55,141
it'd be good if they could take a look
at the opponent's court first,

285
00:12:55,397 --> 00:12:58,210
but in reality,
it's hard to have that moment.

286
00:12:58,844 --> 00:13:03,382
(After ignoring the coach,
the score becomes 8 to 8.)

287
00:13:06,783 --> 00:13:09,588
A quick attack. Myoung-Hwa saved it.

288
00:13:11,114 --> 00:13:12,114
Chae-Rim!

289
00:13:12,258 --> 00:13:14,631
(The libero Sol Min receives it easily.)

290
00:13:14,637 --> 00:13:15,637
Now, it's defense.

291
00:13:17,687 --> 00:13:18,964
To the left.

292
00:13:19,698 --> 00:13:21,466
(Tip counterattack)

293
00:13:24,643 --> 00:13:25,805
Tip it!

294
00:13:28,908 --> 00:13:30,778
(Diving dig)

295
00:13:30,779 --> 00:13:32,452
Diving dig! What an incredible defense!

296
00:13:35,355 --> 00:13:36,435
Na-Yeon, set it up!

297
00:13:37,927 --> 00:13:38,927
Dang it. My arm hurts.

298
00:13:39,334 --> 00:13:40,334
Hey, tip it!

299
00:13:43,022 --> 00:13:46,626
(One block)

300
00:13:47,426 --> 00:13:48,928
(So furious!)

301
00:13:49,529 --> 00:13:52,608
Powerful hit to draw the block!

302
00:13:52,609 --> 00:13:54,904
(Their sadness is our joy.)

303
00:13:58,573 --> 00:14:00,206
The toss isn't looking good right now.

304
00:14:02,181 --> 00:14:07,520
(As the third set began,
her ball connections became unstable.)

305
00:14:10,771 --> 00:14:13,591
Na-Yeon's tosses started to waver,

306
00:14:13,858 --> 00:14:18,558
and points were not coming as they should.

307
00:14:21,782 --> 00:14:23,462
- Now, Jin goes in.
- Jin? Now?

308
00:14:24,009 --> 00:14:25,009
Jin.

309
00:14:26,165 --> 00:14:29,568
(She makes another setter change.)

310
00:14:29,958 --> 00:14:31,704
(Lee Na-Yeon to Lee Jin)

311
00:14:32,452 --> 00:14:33,840
There's a setter change.

312
00:14:34,292 --> 00:14:36,964
Now, Jin steps onto the court
for the first time.

313
00:14:37,643 --> 00:14:41,714
(Will this substitution turn out
to be a blessing or a curse?)

314
00:14:49,255 --> 00:14:50,990
(Jin's back toss)

315
00:14:54,226 --> 00:14:56,428
(The team scored right after Jin came in.)

316
00:14:56,481 --> 00:14:57,896
- Great. I'll make it quicker now.
- Okay.

317
00:14:57,901 --> 00:14:59,808
- Do it more quickly.
- Sure. All right!

318
00:15:01,204 --> 00:15:03,836
Jin delivered the toss to the side
with fewer blockers.

319
00:15:05,504 --> 00:15:08,491
(A precise and powerful back set)

320
00:15:08,524 --> 00:15:11,894
All Wonder Dogs players looked
tense and stiff...

321
00:15:12,147 --> 00:15:14,447
when they first stepped onto the court,

322
00:15:14,640 --> 00:15:16,882
but Jin showed none of that.

323
00:15:17,221 --> 00:15:18,468
Relax, girls!

324
00:15:19,934 --> 00:15:20,934
The score is nine all.

325
00:15:28,323 --> 00:15:29,729
The receive is shaky.

326
00:15:35,234 --> 00:15:37,770
- Great!
- Nice attack!

327
00:15:38,229 --> 00:15:39,960
The players are shouting even
louder to pump themselves up.

328
00:15:39,961 --> 00:15:41,090
Right.

329
00:15:41,874 --> 00:15:43,108
Nice serve!

330
00:15:43,554 --> 00:15:46,174
Sometimes, you need to shout...

331
00:15:46,175 --> 00:15:49,348
- and push yourself to the limit.
- That's right.

332
00:15:51,387 --> 00:15:52,620
(Satisfied)

333
00:15:52,633 --> 00:15:53,986
The Wonder Dogs take the lead
by one point again.

334
00:15:56,725 --> 00:15:59,224
Jin, wait a bit longer.

335
00:15:59,305 --> 00:16:00,926
(Using Jin while she's on a roll)

336
00:16:01,512 --> 00:16:03,796
Don't rush.

337
00:16:05,616 --> 00:16:08,392
Open spike! It's out!

338
00:16:09,043 --> 00:16:11,923
Out! Awesome!

339
00:16:20,488 --> 00:16:23,515
- Enkhsoyol, tip it to position three.
- Okay.

340
00:16:23,535 --> 00:16:25,084
- They're all out in defense.
- Okay.

341
00:16:25,847 --> 00:16:27,880
Hit it confidently.
Even if it gets blocked, hit it hard.

342
00:16:28,214 --> 00:16:30,155
Even if it gets blocked, hit it hard.

343
00:16:33,292 --> 00:16:35,461
(Yeon Koung:
Lightly tip it to position three.)

344
00:16:35,462 --> 00:16:39,532
(Myoung-Hwa: Spike it hard!)

345
00:16:39,965 --> 00:16:44,670
(Did Yes-Enkhsoyol understand
Yeon Koung's instruction?)

346
00:16:54,972 --> 00:16:57,883
- A spike! She saved it.
- The ball is in.

347
00:16:59,304 --> 00:17:00,519
Coach!

348
00:17:01,987 --> 00:17:04,590
(Enkhsoyol is ready for an attack.)

349
00:17:04,623 --> 00:17:05,623
Enkhsoyol!

350
00:17:05,624 --> 00:17:08,227
(Lightly tip it to position three!)

351
00:17:08,674 --> 00:17:10,028
Smash it!

352
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:13,399
Smash it!

353
00:17:13,867 --> 00:17:16,633
That is a point!

354
00:17:17,169 --> 00:17:19,872
(Tipping over to position three)

355
00:17:26,912 --> 00:17:31,383
(Finally, the strategy worked!)

356
00:17:34,086 --> 00:17:36,055
(Screaming)

357
00:17:39,792 --> 00:17:42,662
(See that?)

358
00:17:44,887 --> 00:17:48,300
Enkhsoyol! Thank you.

359
00:17:48,965 --> 00:17:51,405
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

360
00:17:51,472 --> 00:17:53,172
- Enkhsoyol, that was great!
- Okay.

361
00:18:01,067 --> 00:18:02,067
You saw that, right?

362
00:18:03,494 --> 00:18:07,419
As Wonder Dogs take a 3-point lead
with a score of 16 to 13,

363
00:18:07,977 --> 00:18:10,622
we head into the second technical timeout.

364
00:18:10,623 --> 00:18:12,090
(Technical timeout
since one team won 8 points.)

365
00:18:12,600 --> 00:18:14,767
I'm happy Enkhsoyol regained her smile.

366
00:18:16,780 --> 00:18:18,697
The brighter our faces get,

367
00:18:19,226 --> 00:18:22,167
the darker the face of the Geunyoung High
principal becomes.

368
00:18:25,270 --> 00:18:27,906
(Approaching slowly)

369
00:18:29,058 --> 00:18:30,058
Let's go!

370
00:18:33,621 --> 00:18:34,981
He came closer now.

371
00:18:34,982 --> 00:18:38,450
- When the team is on a roll...
- Manager Boo gets closer to Coach Kim.

372
00:18:38,808 --> 00:18:41,118
Get us water already.
We're running out of time.

373
00:18:43,288 --> 00:18:45,957
(Laughing)

374
00:18:46,693 --> 00:18:48,400
She's smiling now.

375
00:18:48,748 --> 00:18:51,818
The manager Boo's job is
to lift the team's spirit.

376
00:18:52,159 --> 00:18:55,534
- Even Coach Kim can't help but smile.
- He knows how to boost the mood.

377
00:18:56,539 --> 00:18:59,171
- Move quickly.
- Yes, ma'am!

378
00:18:59,696 --> 00:19:00,696
You've got this!

379
00:19:01,569 --> 00:19:03,125
- The score gap isn't big.
- Yes.

380
00:19:03,126 --> 00:19:04,940
- Let's handle it one point at a time.
- Okay!

381
00:19:04,940 --> 00:19:06,062
(After the technical timeout)

382
00:19:06,726 --> 00:19:07,726
Thank you.

383
00:19:08,547 --> 00:19:11,750
(With a score of 15 to 17,
Wonder Dogs are still in the lead.)

384
00:19:12,744 --> 00:19:15,287
I've been thinking
about how to lure the opponents.

385
00:19:16,488 --> 00:19:20,926
(Watching the opponent's court carefully)

386
00:19:21,624 --> 00:19:22,624
Position one.

387
00:19:22,649 --> 00:19:24,630
(Position one)

388
00:19:25,762 --> 00:19:26,762
Listen.

389
00:19:28,562 --> 00:19:31,036
If you're a server in this situation,
you're very lucky.

390
00:19:32,891 --> 00:19:35,617
The server is a lucky one.
Do you know why?

391
00:19:36,682 --> 00:19:39,496
If the players with a powerful spike
smash the ball our way,

392
00:19:40,289 --> 00:19:41,621
then...

393
00:19:43,195 --> 00:19:45,830
that's the start of our scoring spree.

394
00:19:46,321 --> 00:19:47,276
- Right?
- Yes.

395
00:19:47,277 --> 00:19:49,234
Enkhsoyol, you know what to do
when you serve tomorrow, right?

396
00:19:49,235 --> 00:19:51,035
(You know what to do, Enkhsoyol.)

397
00:19:51,791 --> 00:19:52,791
Number 1.

398
00:19:52,791 --> 00:19:57,258
(Player 4 is in zone 1.)

399
00:19:57,258 --> 00:19:58,525
All right.

400
00:19:58,525 --> 00:20:00,125
(A dialect from Mokpo)

401
00:20:00,525 --> 00:20:02,425
(It's their rare chance
to serve endlessly.)

402
00:20:02,425 --> 00:20:03,491
Serve!

403
00:20:07,991 --> 00:20:09,025
A serve error.

404
00:20:09,025 --> 00:20:10,325
(Dumbfounded)

405
00:20:10,325 --> 00:20:12,191
- Again!
- Okay.

406
00:20:12,191 --> 00:20:13,791
(Sighing)

407
00:20:13,791 --> 00:20:14,891
(This is making me crazy.)

408
00:20:15,958 --> 00:20:17,858
I'll need a drink today.

409
00:20:18,925 --> 00:20:21,391
No player wants to make an error.

410
00:20:21,825 --> 00:20:24,791
- But now isn't the time to make mistakes.
- That's right.

411
00:20:25,591 --> 00:20:27,525
We can catch up. Let's go.

412
00:20:30,291 --> 00:20:31,725
They're only one point apart.

413
00:20:32,425 --> 00:20:33,525
Ban Ye Bin serves.

414
00:20:36,291 --> 00:20:37,325
Reception is unstable.

415
00:20:39,525 --> 00:20:40,591
Using an underhand toss.

416
00:20:43,658 --> 00:20:44,658
(Blocking the tip)

417
00:20:44,658 --> 00:20:46,391
She received it.

418
00:20:46,391 --> 00:20:47,391
That's it!

419
00:20:51,258 --> 00:20:52,725
- Touch!
- Let's go!

420
00:20:52,725 --> 00:20:54,691
It's their chance to tie the game.
Standing spike!

421
00:20:59,258 --> 00:21:00,425
It's okay.

422
00:21:00,425 --> 00:21:01,891
(They're now tied
after allowing a touch-out.)

423
00:21:02,858 --> 00:21:04,625
(We got them!)

424
00:21:04,625 --> 00:21:07,291
Geunyoung Girls' High doesn't miss
their chance.

425
00:21:07,291 --> 00:21:10,291
(Third set, Geunyoung Girls' High 17
: Wonder Dogs 17)

426
00:21:10,591 --> 00:21:12,091
It's 17 to 17.

427
00:21:12,091 --> 00:21:15,325
Wonder Dogs allow the score
to be tied once again.

428
00:21:15,325 --> 00:21:16,391
Look at the first serve.

429
00:21:16,391 --> 00:21:19,491
(Will they lose again by a comeback
just like in the second set?)

430
00:21:20,091 --> 00:21:21,191
Ban Ye Bin serves.

431
00:21:22,758 --> 00:21:24,725
Their reception is unstable again.

432
00:21:24,725 --> 00:21:25,958
Use a tip!

433
00:21:25,958 --> 00:21:27,091
Tip!

434
00:21:27,391 --> 00:21:28,825
They blocked it with a tip.

435
00:21:33,125 --> 00:21:34,158
Hit it!

436
00:21:34,158 --> 00:21:35,158
Watch the soft hit!

437
00:21:38,458 --> 00:21:40,091
A soft spike and back to the defense line.

438
00:21:40,091 --> 00:21:41,658
Geunyoung Girls' High might turn
the tables.

439
00:21:41,658 --> 00:21:44,325
(It's their big shot to break the tie!)

440
00:21:48,325 --> 00:21:49,891
- She saved it!
- Nice!

441
00:21:50,058 --> 00:21:52,391
(Did Enkhsoyol save the ball?)

442
00:21:52,791 --> 00:21:55,025
(The hellish defense battle)

443
00:21:55,191 --> 00:21:56,625
(Get the ball over first.)

444
00:21:57,391 --> 00:21:59,425
- A free ball!
- Gosh.

445
00:21:59,925 --> 00:22:02,758
(Save the free ball!)

446
00:22:03,125 --> 00:22:05,258
Go straight!

447
00:22:09,791 --> 00:22:12,391
(In)

448
00:22:13,225 --> 00:22:15,191
It goes to the right, and they score!

449
00:22:15,191 --> 00:22:17,158
They take back the lead.

450
00:22:17,591 --> 00:22:19,725
Yoo Da Eun, the problem solver
of Geunyoung Girls' High.

451
00:22:21,025 --> 00:22:22,091
Great job!

452
00:22:22,558 --> 00:22:26,025
(Geunyoung Girls' High takes
the lead back.)

453
00:22:26,491 --> 00:22:27,625
(Laughing)

454
00:22:27,625 --> 00:22:29,658
- We changed the game!
- Yeah, we did.

455
00:22:33,658 --> 00:22:36,258
(Wonder Dogs are once again overtaken
towards the end of the set.)

456
00:22:36,258 --> 00:22:39,225
You can hear the ball
thudding loudly on the court, right?

457
00:22:39,225 --> 00:22:41,491
It's very powerful.

458
00:22:43,491 --> 00:22:44,625
Please.

459
00:22:47,191 --> 00:22:50,658
She'll obviously miss the ball
if you pass it like that!

460
00:22:51,458 --> 00:22:52,491
What's wrong with her?

461
00:22:54,758 --> 00:22:55,991
(Walking on eggshells)

462
00:22:55,991 --> 00:22:59,158
The coaching staff is
all watching Coach Kim.

463
00:22:59,158 --> 00:23:03,225
They set their eyes on her
and are reading the atmosphere.

464
00:23:03,225 --> 00:23:06,491
Although they have done nothing wrong,
they're still watching her.

465
00:23:08,625 --> 00:23:10,791
- You can be a good manager.
- I know, right?

466
00:23:11,258 --> 00:23:13,558
Young In, why aren't you ready?
You can't hit the ball just once.

467
00:23:14,558 --> 00:23:16,925
Enkhsoyol, I told you it's empty!

468
00:23:17,191 --> 00:23:19,325
Before we even realized,

469
00:23:19,458 --> 00:23:23,091
Manager Boo began to keep
his distance from Coach Kim.

470
00:23:24,658 --> 00:23:27,158
(The competitive boss)

471
00:23:27,158 --> 00:23:29,225
Receive it!

472
00:23:30,358 --> 00:23:31,558
It's empty in the middle!

473
00:23:35,125 --> 00:23:36,625
(They lose a point.)

474
00:23:36,625 --> 00:23:37,891
It's a serve attack.

475
00:23:41,991 --> 00:23:43,225
(She gets angrier for a point lost.)

476
00:23:43,225 --> 00:23:45,591
Jin, focus on the main hitter
if you want to play safe.

477
00:23:45,591 --> 00:23:47,091
- Go for her!
- Understood.

478
00:23:51,791 --> 00:23:54,358
- They blocked it tightly!
- What a solid block.

479
00:23:54,358 --> 00:23:56,191
They did it at the crucial moment.

480
00:23:56,191 --> 00:23:57,291
You're right.

481
00:23:59,025 --> 00:24:01,391
The ball is in!

482
00:24:02,225 --> 00:24:03,291
Hey!

483
00:24:05,758 --> 00:24:08,291
(An emotional rollercoaster
with each point)

484
00:24:08,991 --> 00:24:11,958
Her eyebags are darker
than at the start of the game.

485
00:24:13,225 --> 00:24:18,358
Wonder Dogs must win four games
out of seven.

486
00:24:18,591 --> 00:24:21,225
Each set matters greatly to them.

487
00:24:22,191 --> 00:24:23,825
It's 23 to 22.

488
00:24:24,325 --> 00:24:25,625
Listen. Come here.

489
00:24:26,225 --> 00:24:27,758
See? It's open there.

490
00:24:27,758 --> 00:24:29,325
I told you so many times.

491
00:24:29,425 --> 00:24:31,625
Keep attacking zone 3 until it works.

492
00:24:31,625 --> 00:24:32,758
- Yes.
- Did it work?

493
00:24:32,891 --> 00:24:34,358
- It did.
- Don't stop the attack.

494
00:24:34,358 --> 00:24:35,525
- Until you score.
- Yes.

495
00:24:35,525 --> 00:24:36,925
- Use that zone.
- Understood.

496
00:24:37,425 --> 00:24:38,891
You're high school students.

497
00:24:38,891 --> 00:24:40,058
There's nothing to lose.

498
00:24:40,058 --> 00:24:41,125
There isn't.

499
00:24:41,391 --> 00:24:42,591
Geunyoung.

500
00:24:43,158 --> 00:24:46,358
"Nothing to lose" can be Geunyoung Girls'
High's most formidable mindset.

501
00:24:46,358 --> 00:24:47,358
You're right.

502
00:24:47,725 --> 00:24:48,891
Let's go for more points.

503
00:24:49,625 --> 00:24:50,625
Thank you.

504
00:24:50,858 --> 00:24:53,425
(Underdogs can't lose more.)

505
00:24:58,958 --> 00:25:01,658
From now on, they must not...

506
00:25:01,658 --> 00:25:03,725
- make any error.
- They shouldn't.

507
00:25:08,458 --> 00:25:09,458
Serve!

508
00:25:09,458 --> 00:25:10,491
(Yoo Da Eun serves.)

509
00:25:12,591 --> 00:25:13,691
It hits the net.

510
00:25:14,358 --> 00:25:15,491
The net!

511
00:25:17,558 --> 00:25:19,291
(Hye In's determined reception)

512
00:25:19,958 --> 00:25:21,091
She received the ball.

513
00:25:24,358 --> 00:25:25,458
Enkhsoyol!

514
00:25:29,058 --> 00:25:30,225
Tip it.

515
00:25:30,891 --> 00:25:32,358
Please!

516
00:25:35,577 --> 00:25:36,844
That's it!

517
00:25:37,436 --> 00:25:38,436
Nice!

518
00:25:38,436 --> 00:25:39,669
Enkhsoyol!

519
00:25:39,669 --> 00:25:41,403
(A tip attack to zone 3)

520
00:25:41,403 --> 00:25:42,436
Zone 3!

521
00:25:46,036 --> 00:25:47,036
Nice!

522
00:25:47,036 --> 00:25:48,236
Enkhsoyol!

523
00:25:49,469 --> 00:25:51,536
(Thrilling)

524
00:25:52,803 --> 00:25:53,836
Enkhsoyol.

525
00:25:54,269 --> 00:25:55,669
I told you you could score.

526
00:25:55,803 --> 00:25:58,103
If you can't, just pass it to others.

527
00:25:58,103 --> 00:25:59,503
This is a key point.

528
00:26:00,403 --> 00:26:01,669
One more point!

529
00:26:01,669 --> 00:26:02,936
- Nice one, Enkhsoyol!
- Okay!

530
00:26:03,536 --> 00:26:05,403
That was a great defense.

531
00:26:06,503 --> 00:26:08,703
Enkhsoyol doesn't go for this spot.

532
00:26:09,436 --> 00:26:12,303
(Watch out for the tip attack to zone 3.)

533
00:26:12,303 --> 00:26:16,503
As Enkhsoyol scores a crucial point,

534
00:26:16,503 --> 00:26:19,669
Wonder Dogs enter set point
in the third set.

535
00:26:19,969 --> 00:26:22,536
(One more point,
and we will win the third set.)

536
00:26:22,536 --> 00:26:25,136
One point!

537
00:26:25,136 --> 00:26:26,503
Just one more!

538
00:26:26,503 --> 00:26:28,936
One point!

539
00:26:31,769 --> 00:26:33,136
(A quick attack)

540
00:26:33,136 --> 00:26:35,003
A quick attack in the middle,
blocked by the defenders!

541
00:26:35,003 --> 00:26:36,436
Enkhsoyol, hit it!

542
00:26:37,669 --> 00:26:40,136
(Enkhsoyol gets ready.)

543
00:26:40,503 --> 00:26:41,636
The front!

544
00:26:41,736 --> 00:26:43,203
(Preparing for a tip attack in zone 3)

545
00:26:48,536 --> 00:26:51,269
(The ball is in the air.)

546
00:26:52,669 --> 00:26:54,803
Enkhsoyol, their defenders are all out.

547
00:26:55,536 --> 00:26:58,336
(For Enkhsoyol, who's from Mongolia,)

548
00:26:58,436 --> 00:27:01,369
(Coach Kim even bends forward
to instruct a tip to zone 3.)

549
00:27:01,869 --> 00:27:04,669
(She repeats "tip to zone 3"
until her voice is hoarse.)

550
00:27:04,669 --> 00:27:07,736
- Use that zone.
- Yes. Understood.

551
00:27:07,936 --> 00:27:09,636
Do you understand?

552
00:27:12,236 --> 00:27:13,303
Yes!

553
00:27:13,803 --> 00:27:16,536
Enkhsoyol pulls off her push shot!

554
00:27:19,836 --> 00:27:20,969
Yeah!

555
00:27:21,536 --> 00:27:23,636
Great job.

556
00:27:25,503 --> 00:27:29,169
(Geunyoung Girls' High 22: Wonder Dogs 25)

557
00:27:31,869 --> 00:27:32,969
That was perfect.

558
00:27:36,169 --> 00:27:38,203
What a master of tips, Enkhsoyol.

559
00:27:38,203 --> 00:27:39,803
- Way to go, Enkhsoyol!
- So awesome.

560
00:27:39,803 --> 00:27:40,969
- That was so good.
- All of them fell for it.

561
00:27:40,969 --> 00:27:43,503
Enkhsoyol made the third set hers!

562
00:27:44,169 --> 00:27:47,103
I'll put my pillow on zone 3 today.

563
00:27:48,336 --> 00:27:51,236
And I'll sleep on zone 3 as well.

564
00:27:52,336 --> 00:27:54,069
(Timeout for the fourth set)

565
00:27:54,969 --> 00:27:56,703
- Serve with more power!
- Yes.

566
00:27:56,703 --> 00:27:57,869
Why are you so weak? Didn't you practice?

567
00:27:57,869 --> 00:27:58,936
We did.

568
00:27:58,936 --> 00:28:00,769
We're all checking on you.

569
00:28:00,769 --> 00:28:02,169
If you miss the serve,

570
00:28:02,169 --> 00:28:05,503
you'll lose a point in no time.

571
00:28:05,503 --> 00:28:07,203
Serve harder.

572
00:28:07,203 --> 00:28:08,203
Yes.

573
00:28:08,203 --> 00:28:09,303
(Keeping up the momentum
and hustling players)

574
00:28:09,536 --> 00:28:11,336
- It's not over yet.
- Understood.

575
00:28:11,969 --> 00:28:14,503
Strong teams can beat them at this point.

576
00:28:14,503 --> 00:28:16,169
But weak teams will be defeated.

577
00:28:16,169 --> 00:28:17,203
Yes.

578
00:28:18,236 --> 00:28:19,769
- Let's do our best.
- Yes, Coach!

579
00:28:19,769 --> 00:28:21,269
Geunyoung!

580
00:28:22,003 --> 00:28:25,036
Wonder Dogs must finish the game
in the fourth set.

581
00:28:25,036 --> 00:28:26,136
You're correct.

582
00:28:26,136 --> 00:28:27,903
(They must win this set
to secure their victory.)

583
00:28:28,603 --> 00:28:31,203
(The first one to serve is...)

584
00:28:31,803 --> 00:28:34,169
(Coach Kim's favorite student...)

585
00:28:34,169 --> 00:28:36,769
(Enkhsoyol.)

586
00:28:37,636 --> 00:28:38,769
(Lee Da On, her serve target)

587
00:28:40,743 --> 00:28:41,743
Enkhsoyol.

588
00:28:41,744 --> 00:28:44,292
(Aim for zone one)

589
00:28:45,366 --> 00:28:47,829
(On the previous serve,)

590
00:28:49,898 --> 00:28:53,268
(she failed to hit her target, zone one.)

591
00:28:54,503 --> 00:28:57,840
- Let's make sure we pass.
- Let's go!

592
00:28:58,144 --> 00:28:59,144
Watch out for a short one.

593
00:28:59,145 --> 00:29:00,876
(Nodding)

594
00:29:01,180 --> 00:29:03,980
- One, two, three. Nice serve!
- Nice serve!

595
00:29:04,263 --> 00:29:06,615
Set four begins with Enkhsoyol's serve.

596
00:29:06,773 --> 00:29:07,773
What was that serve?

597
00:29:08,606 --> 00:29:11,620
What was that serve? Are you kidding me?

598
00:29:12,988 --> 00:29:14,056
(Ball flying)

599
00:29:14,556 --> 00:29:16,758
(It got blocked because it was too weak.)

600
00:29:18,322 --> 00:29:19,322
They're passing it high.

601
00:29:20,468 --> 00:29:21,914
- Ball goes out.
- Yes.

602
00:29:25,184 --> 00:29:27,011
- What's with that serve?
- I missed it.

603
00:29:27,247 --> 00:29:28,247
You can do this!

604
00:29:31,280 --> 00:29:32,790
- Hey!
- Yes, coach.

605
00:29:34,533 --> 00:29:35,533
Yes, coach.

606
00:29:36,211 --> 00:29:39,794
I feel like she's going to have a meltdown
after this game today.

607
00:29:40,115 --> 00:29:42,517
(Trying to stay calm)

608
00:29:44,479 --> 00:29:46,722
- One, two, three! Nice serve!
- Nice serve!

609
00:29:49,839 --> 00:29:50,839
What?

610
00:29:51,226 --> 00:29:53,528
(Serve completely off the target)

611
00:29:54,904 --> 00:29:56,457
Block on the right side.

612
00:30:01,044 --> 00:30:03,104
- All right.
- She's chasing the ball!

613
00:30:04,196 --> 00:30:06,056
They failed to save it.

614
00:30:06,623 --> 00:30:07,623
Hey!

615
00:30:10,345 --> 00:30:12,681
(Point to Geunyoung Girls' High)

616
00:30:12,873 --> 00:30:14,152
Nice.

617
00:30:16,578 --> 00:30:18,753
- What are you doing, Myoung-Hwa?
- It was a mistake.

618
00:30:19,345 --> 00:30:20,956
That wasn't a mistake, you know that.

619
00:30:22,488 --> 00:30:24,642
When the ball goes far,

620
00:30:24,715 --> 00:30:27,631
everyone needs to move towards it.

621
00:30:27,658 --> 00:30:30,198
Well, Myoung-Hwa is a player
with a lot of advantages,

622
00:30:30,199 --> 00:30:32,584
but her only downside is speed.

623
00:30:33,253 --> 00:30:34,740
Myoung-Hwa, you're too slow.

624
00:30:38,006 --> 00:30:41,443
(Fourth set, Geunyoung Girls' High 1
: Wonder Dogs 1)

625
00:30:42,144 --> 00:30:45,447
(Yoon Hwa's serve)

626
00:30:48,269 --> 00:30:49,269
Nice catch!

627
00:30:49,408 --> 00:30:50,885
Hit it! In between!

628
00:30:51,486 --> 00:30:52,932
(Chae Rim's strong spike)

629
00:30:52,952 --> 00:30:53,952
A strong spike!

630
00:30:56,658 --> 00:30:58,894
(Soo Min's strong spike)

631
00:31:01,029 --> 00:31:03,665
(It's a tight game.)

632
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:06,301
(Send it over!)

633
00:31:07,673 --> 00:31:08,673
Set it up!

634
00:31:10,129 --> 00:31:11,129
Hit it!

635
00:31:11,536 --> 00:31:13,508
Tip to zone three! Zone three!

636
00:31:16,676 --> 00:31:18,896
Pushing it to the right!

637
00:31:19,748 --> 00:31:22,025
They hit zone three and scored again!

638
00:31:22,026 --> 00:31:23,952
That's it!

639
00:31:23,992 --> 00:31:25,592
- Young In's got it.
- She's in the flow.

640
00:31:26,292 --> 00:31:28,205
- Nice one, Jin.
- Was that okay?

641
00:31:28,285 --> 00:31:30,059
Young In, nice.

642
00:31:31,411 --> 00:31:32,435
Jin, you did great too.

643
00:31:33,052 --> 00:31:36,882
- Jin, plan it with Young In.
- Yes, coach.

644
00:31:37,899 --> 00:31:39,801
(Jin is exchanging signals with Young In.)

645
00:31:42,291 --> 00:31:44,973
Right back strike, and it's a point.

646
00:31:45,903 --> 00:31:49,444
They toss it and hit it strong! Nice!

647
00:31:50,879 --> 00:31:52,105
(Geunyoung Girls' High 3: Wonder Dogs 6)

648
00:31:52,106 --> 00:31:53,363
We're on a roll!

649
00:31:56,136 --> 00:31:59,154
A back attack from the middle.
Point for Wonder Dogs!

650
00:32:01,428 --> 00:32:03,520
They blocked it. Jin's blocking!

651
00:32:04,468 --> 00:32:05,468
Yes, Jin!

652
00:32:08,009 --> 00:32:11,102
That was a great block,
bringing up the team's morale!

653
00:32:12,145 --> 00:32:13,369
- Nice going, Jin!
- Yes.

654
00:32:15,670 --> 00:32:18,640
(Jin was known more
for her looks than her skills,)

655
00:32:19,207 --> 00:32:22,343
(but she never gave up on her dream
to play in the pro league again.)

656
00:32:22,911 --> 00:32:25,580
(She's eager to prove her talent now.)

657
00:32:26,989 --> 00:32:28,629
- It's a short one!
- Watch out!

658
00:32:28,649 --> 00:32:30,068
Oh, gosh. Please!

659
00:32:35,171 --> 00:32:37,691
I still have so much to show.

660
00:32:43,298 --> 00:32:46,334
(Jin's fake feint)

661
00:32:51,162 --> 00:32:52,162
Nice!

662
00:32:55,562 --> 00:32:59,514
I could tell that Jin understood the most
and came prepared.

663
00:33:00,241 --> 00:33:03,585
I thought the coach's instructions were
always on point,

664
00:33:03,586 --> 00:33:05,787
so I tried to follow them
as much as possible.

665
00:33:06,880 --> 00:33:09,406
I only thought
about doing my part on the court.

666
00:33:09,407 --> 00:33:11,526
(She fulfilled her role perfectly
on the court.)

667
00:33:14,735 --> 00:33:16,319
It's 12 to 17, a five-point difference.

668
00:33:16,838 --> 00:33:18,725
We have to keep this up.

669
00:33:19,686 --> 00:33:21,339
Prepare for offense.

670
00:33:22,423 --> 00:33:24,663
- One, two, three. Nice serve!
- Nice serve!

671
00:33:26,712 --> 00:33:27,712
- It's out!
- Nice!

672
00:33:28,839 --> 00:33:29,839
- It's out!
- Nice!

673
00:33:30,089 --> 00:33:31,422
That was too much power.

674
00:33:31,423 --> 00:33:33,348
- Nice!
- We can do this!

675
00:33:34,916 --> 00:33:37,085
(Giving her a look)

676
00:33:39,355 --> 00:33:40,888
- No!
- Sorry.

677
00:33:42,858 --> 00:33:45,661
(Starting with Jin's serve error...)

678
00:33:50,327 --> 00:33:54,697
- Spike from the right side!
- That's an error.

679
00:33:55,470 --> 00:33:57,572
(Things are not going well.)

680
00:33:58,243 --> 00:34:02,677
Look, I told you to aim for zone three.
How many times do I have to tell you?

681
00:34:02,806 --> 00:34:05,380
Trust me on this! It'll work!

682
00:34:07,816 --> 00:34:10,786
(Another serve error,
even before they try to hit zone three)

683
00:34:14,122 --> 00:34:16,273
(And a net violation)

684
00:34:16,274 --> 00:34:17,792
It touched the net.

685
00:34:18,226 --> 00:34:21,596
(Nice net violation.
That was over the net.)

686
00:34:22,559 --> 00:34:25,300
With that last net violation,
it's 14 to 14 now.

687
00:34:26,192 --> 00:34:28,570
- They turned a five-point gap into a tie.
- Serve.

688
00:34:28,571 --> 00:34:30,605
(If they lose this point,
they'll be overtaken.)

689
00:34:36,912 --> 00:34:39,197
(No touch. Point to Geunyoung Girls' High)

690
00:34:39,209 --> 00:34:41,349
- It's back to a tie.
- They lost the point.

691
00:34:41,553 --> 00:34:44,283
We're seeing reversals
at crucial moments in every set.

692
00:34:45,083 --> 00:34:46,236
Wonder Dogs are in a crisis.

693
00:34:46,388 --> 00:34:48,800
(Wonder Dogs desperately need a point.)

694
00:34:48,801 --> 00:34:49,801
The pass was too short.

695
00:34:53,595 --> 00:34:56,798
(The blocked ball goes right out.)

696
00:34:58,133 --> 00:35:01,670
(Outstanding play by Soo Min and Eun Chae)

697
00:35:02,301 --> 00:35:04,436
Hey, Soo Min! My, gosh!

698
00:35:06,744 --> 00:35:07,924
That was a perfect play.

699
00:35:07,925 --> 00:35:10,479
(The momentum shifts back
to Geunyoung Girls' High.)

700
00:35:15,483 --> 00:35:16,483
No...

701
00:35:17,855 --> 00:35:22,190
Geunyoung Girls' High is leading
by two points, 16 to 14.

702
00:35:24,793 --> 00:35:28,096
(Technical timeout)

703
00:35:28,927 --> 00:35:31,934
- What do you do when you're cornered?
- Pass it long.

704
00:35:32,047 --> 00:35:33,760
- Or?
- Tip to zone three.

705
00:35:34,007 --> 00:35:36,997
I told you to go for the tip.
Don't waste plays.

706
00:35:36,998 --> 00:35:39,618
- Tip it, and we'll get another chance.
- Yes, coach.

707
00:35:39,631 --> 00:35:42,491
- Don't try to finish it off at once.
- Yes, coach.

708
00:35:44,737 --> 00:35:46,448
- Let's go, girls!
- We got this!

709
00:35:46,681 --> 00:35:49,817
(Deep in thoughts)

710
00:35:50,385 --> 00:35:51,586
Jin.

711
00:35:51,820 --> 00:35:53,088
Go with a back C.

712
00:35:53,507 --> 00:35:55,590
- Back C, and pass it to Young In.
- Okay.

713
00:35:56,825 --> 00:36:01,430
(Depending on the setter's toss distance,)

714
00:36:02,430 --> 00:36:06,067
(they can play quick attack A, B, or C.)

715
00:36:07,502 --> 00:36:11,606
(If the toss goes as far back as C,
it's called a back C.)

716
00:36:11,763 --> 00:36:13,441
Let's go with back C again.

717
00:36:14,109 --> 00:36:16,778
(Passing on the new tactic with the team)

718
00:36:17,279 --> 00:36:19,948
(They need to close the gap now!)

719
00:36:20,136 --> 00:36:21,136
Serve.

720
00:36:21,137 --> 00:36:23,285
(Another serve by Yoon Ha)

721
00:36:25,872 --> 00:36:26,872
It hit the net.

722
00:36:27,579 --> 00:36:28,579
That's a nice pass.

723
00:36:30,191 --> 00:36:31,659
Play back C.

724
00:36:31,660 --> 00:36:33,095
(They have to send it back to back C.)

725
00:36:33,795 --> 00:36:36,331
(Zone three is completely open.)

726
00:36:36,364 --> 00:36:40,835
(Will they use the tip
to zone three this time?)

727
00:36:44,183 --> 00:36:45,183
They sent it over.

728
00:36:49,753 --> 00:36:51,259
- All right.
- They did it!

729
00:36:51,333 --> 00:36:52,748
- Tip to zone three!
- Nice!

730
00:36:52,749 --> 00:36:55,050
- That's it!
- Yes!

731
00:36:59,795 --> 00:37:03,591
- Young In, remember. Zone three.
- Yes, coach.

732
00:37:05,121 --> 00:37:07,495
Zone three! To zone three!

733
00:37:08,930 --> 00:37:11,257
(Finally, Wonder Dogs' turn to serve)

734
00:37:11,258 --> 00:37:13,537
- One, two, three! Nice serve!
- Nice serve!

735
00:37:14,469 --> 00:37:16,171
(Standing close to the sideline)

736
00:37:17,273 --> 00:37:18,940
Young In, nice position.

737
00:37:23,259 --> 00:37:24,259
Let's go!

738
00:37:24,833 --> 00:37:26,448
That pass was a bit shaky.

739
00:37:27,816 --> 00:37:29,139
(Soo Min's attack)

740
00:37:29,178 --> 00:37:30,178
It was blocked.

741
00:37:31,005 --> 00:37:32,218
Here it comes again.

742
00:37:35,690 --> 00:37:37,444
(Wonder Dogs score with a block.)

743
00:37:37,470 --> 00:37:40,195
- That was a nice block.
- Yes, nice block!

744
00:37:40,384 --> 00:37:41,384
Way to go!

745
00:37:41,385 --> 00:37:44,299
(It's back to a tie now.)

746
00:37:45,133 --> 00:37:46,851
(Thrilling)

747
00:37:46,852 --> 00:37:48,327
Nice going.

748
00:37:48,867 --> 00:37:49,994
It's 16 to 16.

749
00:37:51,439 --> 00:37:53,941
(Will Geunyoung Girls' High
lose their lead?)

750
00:37:54,476 --> 00:37:57,279
(Will Wonder Dogs take the lead?)

751
00:37:58,446 --> 00:37:59,446
Go!

752
00:38:01,581 --> 00:38:02,801
That was a good serve.

753
00:38:05,144 --> 00:38:06,144
They saved it.

754
00:38:06,145 --> 00:38:08,589
(Setter Jin's first touch)

755
00:38:08,857 --> 00:38:11,126
(The setter can't take
the second ball now.)

756
00:38:11,501 --> 00:38:12,501
Go, Myoung-Hwa!

757
00:38:12,927 --> 00:38:17,398
(Myoung-Hwa is running!)

758
00:38:21,288 --> 00:38:22,604
Second pass by Myoung-Hwa!

759
00:38:25,751 --> 00:38:27,875
A spike from the right!

760
00:38:28,071 --> 00:38:30,378
They're back on a winning streak!

761
00:38:37,042 --> 00:38:39,243
Young In's comeback point!

762
00:38:39,278 --> 00:38:40,778
Jin, nice defense!

763
00:38:40,779 --> 00:38:42,813
Myoung-Hwa, nice set!

764
00:38:42,814 --> 00:38:44,415
Myoung-Hwa!

765
00:38:44,422 --> 00:38:46,217
(Myoung-Hwa, nice job!)

766
00:38:46,558 --> 00:38:48,626
(Yes, that was quite nice!)

767
00:38:50,028 --> 00:38:54,064
(Myoung-Hwa, always called slow,)

768
00:38:55,266 --> 00:38:57,734
(becomes quick in a team crisis!)

769
00:38:57,735 --> 00:39:00,804
Myoung-Hwa set the ball perfectly.

770
00:39:00,805 --> 00:39:03,974
Today, Myoung-Hwa is flawless,
from blocking to connection.

771
00:39:09,481 --> 00:39:10,714
The score is 17 to 16.

772
00:39:11,182 --> 00:39:13,583
The fourth set is entering
the later stages.

773
00:39:13,585 --> 00:39:15,052
(On the edge of their seats)

774
00:39:19,057 --> 00:39:19,890
Young In.

775
00:39:20,125 --> 00:39:23,027
If the situation is tough,
spike toward the corner.

776
00:39:23,027 --> 00:39:24,895
- Spike!
- That was nice.

777
00:39:25,130 --> 00:39:26,964
Young In's clean attack!

778
00:39:27,232 --> 00:39:28,165
Jin.

779
00:39:28,166 --> 00:39:30,601
(When setting, keep it close to the net.)

780
00:39:30,602 --> 00:39:33,471
Chae-Rim drives it down from the left.

781
00:39:33,471 --> 00:39:34,805
(Fourth Set, Geunyoung Girls' High 18
: Wonder Dogs 19)

782
00:39:35,348 --> 00:39:36,806
(Scoring by following
the coach's instructions)

783
00:39:36,841 --> 00:39:40,744
- Back-row power hit!
- Jin, that was amazing!

784
00:39:40,912 --> 00:39:42,512
Spike!

785
00:39:43,047 --> 00:39:45,815
(Geunyoung Girls' High is tough,)

786
00:39:46,651 --> 00:39:48,719
It's 23 to 21, a 2-point lead.

787
00:39:49,505 --> 00:39:52,540
(but Wonder Dogs are
just two points from victory.)

788
00:39:53,224 --> 00:39:55,358
(Na Hee's serve)

789
00:39:55,493 --> 00:39:57,461
I kept thinking...

790
00:39:58,129 --> 00:40:01,565
about what I should do in each situation.

791
00:40:07,872 --> 00:40:08,772
Na Hee.

792
00:40:09,307 --> 00:40:10,140
Okay.

793
00:40:10,742 --> 00:40:13,444
(Instruction received)

794
00:40:14,179 --> 00:40:16,813
(Target zone)

795
00:40:19,651 --> 00:40:21,619
(The ball hit the net?)

796
00:40:24,455 --> 00:40:26,322
The serve hit the net,
and the point goes to Wonder Dogs!

797
00:40:27,826 --> 00:40:30,561
Coach Kim's strategy worked again.

798
00:40:32,697 --> 00:40:34,665
- Nice!
- Let's go!

799
00:40:34,866 --> 00:40:37,000
(The wonderful coach, Yeon Koung)

800
00:40:37,001 --> 00:40:39,002
It's a lucky serve point.

801
00:40:39,003 --> 00:40:40,003
Na Hee, nice!

802
00:40:42,273 --> 00:40:45,943
Now, it's match point
for the Wonder Dogs...

803
00:40:45,944 --> 00:40:48,578
- in their very first game.
- Get it together!

804
00:40:48,579 --> 00:40:49,946
Just one more point!

805
00:40:50,481 --> 00:40:53,884
(The outcome of the game rests
on this one point.)

806
00:40:54,519 --> 00:40:57,154
Jin, send it to middle B.

807
00:40:57,155 --> 00:40:59,923
If not middle B, toss it back.

808
00:41:00,158 --> 00:41:02,326
- Choose either one.
- Okay!

809
00:41:04,495 --> 00:41:06,095
Let's go!

810
00:41:11,202 --> 00:41:13,637
(Setter Jin's choice was...)

811
00:41:15,573 --> 00:41:16,673
She lifted it!

812
00:41:20,578 --> 00:41:22,345
(Young In's spike)

813
00:41:22,347 --> 00:41:24,815
(Did they receive it?)

814
00:41:29,187 --> 00:41:31,422
(It deflected off the player's hand
and left the court.)

815
00:41:31,756 --> 00:41:34,458
Young In's spike!

816
00:41:34,459 --> 00:41:36,860
The score is 22 to 25!

817
00:41:40,765 --> 00:41:42,966
(Wonder Dogs' first victory)

818
00:41:42,967 --> 00:41:43,867
Great!

819
00:41:49,908 --> 00:41:52,076
- Yes!
- Nice!

820
00:41:52,297 --> 00:41:56,053
(Screaming)

821
00:41:56,848 --> 00:42:00,450
Wonder Dogs have claimed
their brilliant first victory.

822
00:42:00,985 --> 00:42:02,419
Good job.

823
00:42:03,054 --> 00:42:05,122
You did so well. I'm sorry.

824
00:42:05,189 --> 00:42:06,556
Jin, well done.

825
00:42:08,626 --> 00:42:10,493
- You all did so great!
- Thank you.

826
00:42:11,396 --> 00:42:12,229
Thank you.

827
00:42:12,230 --> 00:42:13,730
(Geunyoung Girls' High 3 : Wonder Dogs 1)

828
00:42:17,302 --> 00:42:18,235
Nice job.

829
00:42:19,103 --> 00:42:21,371
Nice.

830
00:42:24,175 --> 00:42:26,576
Yeon Koung's debut as coach!

831
00:42:27,111 --> 00:42:31,081
Wonder Dogs win their inaugural match.

832
00:42:31,516 --> 00:42:33,750
It wasn't an easy game,

833
00:42:33,751 --> 00:42:36,753
but Wonder Dogs made it happen.

834
00:42:36,754 --> 00:42:40,123
(Geunyoung Girls' High 3 : Wonder Dogs 1)

835
00:42:40,124 --> 00:42:42,359
- Good game.
- Good job.

836
00:42:42,860 --> 00:42:44,160
Good game.

837
00:42:44,162 --> 00:42:45,129
It was a good game.

838
00:42:46,731 --> 00:42:47,798
- Congratulations.
- I'm delighted.

839
00:42:47,799 --> 00:42:49,333
- Why?
- Your girls are really good.

840
00:42:49,634 --> 00:42:51,435
Thanks. We'll work harder.

841
00:42:51,436 --> 00:42:52,336
They're so good.

842
00:42:52,637 --> 00:42:53,537
Good job.

843
00:42:56,975 --> 00:42:59,410
It felt a little different than usual.

844
00:42:59,411 --> 00:43:01,345
I wasn't that excited about winning,

845
00:43:01,345 --> 00:43:02,345
but I was rather relieved.

846
00:43:02,346 --> 00:43:05,381
I thought, "We got through a tough game.
We won, anyway."

847
00:43:05,383 --> 00:43:07,718
I'm so happy we won.

848
00:43:07,718 --> 00:43:10,220
I'm satisfied with the win,

849
00:43:10,722 --> 00:43:12,756
but I wasn't fully satisfied.

850
00:43:12,757 --> 00:43:20,096
It's because not every player showed
100 percent of their ability.

851
00:43:20,098 --> 00:43:23,033
If we play like this in future matches,

852
00:43:23,534 --> 00:43:24,467
we will lose 100 percent.

853
00:43:28,706 --> 00:43:30,674
(One win in one match achieved)

854
00:43:30,675 --> 00:43:32,843
(The current win rate is 100 percent.)

855
00:43:33,177 --> 00:43:35,445
- Now, we will announce the next opponent.
- Okay.

856
00:43:40,852 --> 00:43:42,419
Hi.

857
00:43:43,221 --> 00:43:45,989
I'm Lee Jin, a setter.

858
00:43:46,624 --> 00:43:48,024
I'm Lee Jin, a setter.

859
00:43:48,559 --> 00:43:51,828
I'm a rookie, but I'll give my best...

860
00:43:52,196 --> 00:43:54,531
to deliver good results.

861
00:43:55,199 --> 00:43:57,133
Hello, I'm Choi Su Bin.

862
00:44:00,238 --> 00:44:02,306
I'm Koo Hye In.

863
00:44:02,673 --> 00:44:03,606
I can't watch.

864
00:44:04,976 --> 00:44:08,745
I'll always show you my bright
and hardworking side,

865
00:44:08,746 --> 00:44:10,146
so please cheer for me a lot.

866
00:44:10,148 --> 00:44:11,982
You'll still be here ten years
from now, right?

867
00:44:13,384 --> 00:44:15,085
(Released in 2025)

868
00:44:15,086 --> 00:44:16,887
(Released in 2023)

869
00:44:17,021 --> 00:44:18,688
(Released in 2023)

870
00:44:20,258 --> 00:44:24,461
(It was once the stage of their dreams.)

871
00:44:25,239 --> 00:44:27,607
(The Altos, a pro volleyball team)

872
00:44:27,632 --> 00:44:30,601
(An integrated champion just two years
after its foundation)

873
00:44:34,672 --> 00:44:37,174
(Won the KOVO Cup Championship,)

874
00:44:37,633 --> 00:44:41,536
(and are currently the strongest
in the league)

875
00:44:42,914 --> 00:44:45,349
The team released me.

876
00:44:45,550 --> 00:44:47,351
"I desperately want to beat them."

877
00:44:47,351 --> 00:44:48,451
That's all I had in my head.

878
00:44:49,797 --> 00:44:51,564
(And the head coach of the Altos,)

879
00:44:51,589 --> 00:44:54,024
(Kim Ho Chul)

880
00:44:54,292 --> 00:44:57,094
(He has a notable history.)

881
00:44:57,562 --> 00:45:00,797
During a complaint, an argument arose
between Yeon Koung and Coach Kim Ho Chul.

882
00:45:00,798 --> 00:45:03,700
(A clash between Yeon Koung
and Kim Ho Chul)

883
00:45:03,935 --> 00:45:08,471
Yeon Koung said that she wasn't
directing her words at the coach.

884
00:45:08,472 --> 00:45:11,774
(An unusual incident where a player
and coach confronted each other)

885
00:45:12,477 --> 00:45:14,344
(Kim Ho Chul and Yeon Koung clear things
up after the argument)

886
00:45:14,345 --> 00:45:17,347
(A hot topic in the volleyball world
that set social media on fire)

887
00:45:20,451 --> 00:45:22,352
(Rookie coach vs. 30-year veteran coach)

888
00:45:22,753 --> 00:45:25,388
(Seven days before the match)

889
00:45:25,923 --> 00:45:26,856
Hi.

890
00:45:27,292 --> 00:45:29,893
I'm coach of the Altos, Kim Ho Chul.

891
00:45:30,437 --> 00:45:32,772
(What do you think
of Coach Kim Yeon Koung?)

892
00:45:32,797 --> 00:45:35,866
From what I've seen,
she was very hot-tempered as a player...

893
00:45:36,068 --> 00:45:40,604
and had a strong competitive spirit,
hating to lose.

894
00:45:40,605 --> 00:45:43,006
She's probably the same as a coach.

895
00:45:43,407 --> 00:45:45,475
That side of her won't change.

896
00:45:46,544 --> 00:45:49,012
(What do you think of Coach Kim Ho Chul?)

897
00:45:49,547 --> 00:45:50,780
(Smiling)

898
00:45:53,884 --> 00:45:55,084
Well...

899
00:45:55,086 --> 00:45:57,621
he's the type to lose his temper easily.
Maybe?

900
00:45:58,055 --> 00:46:00,757
(Laughing)

901
00:46:02,260 --> 00:46:04,828
Coach Kim Ho Chul had been...

902
00:46:04,829 --> 00:46:09,232
coaching in the men's V-League
for a long time too...

903
00:46:09,834 --> 00:46:13,403
and has extensive experience as a coach.

904
00:46:14,039 --> 00:46:16,440
If a player becomes a coach
immediately after retiring,

905
00:46:16,440 --> 00:46:19,142
it's not as easy as it might seem.

906
00:46:19,443 --> 00:46:21,010
Yeon Koung was an outstanding player.

907
00:46:21,445 --> 00:46:22,779
Because she has
a lot of playing experience,

908
00:46:22,780 --> 00:46:24,481
she'll probably think
that she knows a lot.

909
00:46:24,916 --> 00:46:26,583
But that can easily lead to mistakes...

910
00:46:27,218 --> 00:46:31,354
because being a player
and being a coach are very different.

911
00:46:31,722 --> 00:46:34,391
Coaches who were former attackers...

912
00:46:34,392 --> 00:46:37,260
usually prefer
an aggressive style of volleyball.

913
00:46:37,261 --> 00:46:41,698
So I think she'll also pursue
an attack-oriented style.

914
00:46:42,266 --> 00:46:44,234
On the other hand,
coaches who were setters...

915
00:46:44,602 --> 00:46:46,670
tend to look at the game
more strategically.

916
00:46:47,071 --> 00:46:48,371
I'm a former setter myself,

917
00:46:48,372 --> 00:46:49,539
(A legendary setter...)

918
00:46:49,874 --> 00:46:53,610
(who topped Korean men's volleyball
and conquered the European leagues)

919
00:46:53,611 --> 00:46:55,312
and I focus on the overall picture,

920
00:46:55,313 --> 00:46:57,981
like how we should play and how to respond
to the opponent's plays.

921
00:46:57,982 --> 00:47:01,284
One exceptional player alone cannot
make the team shine.

922
00:47:01,419 --> 00:47:05,155
I'd actually been a setter
until middle school.

923
00:47:05,223 --> 00:47:06,924
I was an outside hitter,

924
00:47:06,924 --> 00:47:09,125
but when I played in overseas leagues,

925
00:47:09,126 --> 00:47:13,429
I learned the strategies and instructions
that coaches gave to setters.

926
00:47:13,431 --> 00:47:15,932
I'm passing those on to my players now.

927
00:47:15,933 --> 00:47:20,269
It's not my position,
but I'm confident in teaching them.

928
00:47:20,705 --> 00:47:23,173
I'm confident...

929
00:47:23,574 --> 00:47:26,175
our team will win.

930
00:47:26,377 --> 00:47:28,812
(Laughing)

931
00:47:28,813 --> 00:47:32,449
Since I didn't lose a single match...

932
00:47:32,617 --> 00:47:35,952
against the Altos last season,

933
00:47:36,320 --> 00:47:38,254
I believe our team will perform well too.

934
00:47:39,957 --> 00:47:44,661
(Episode 2,
"Volleyball Is All About the Setter")

935
00:47:44,662 --> 00:47:47,964
Our next opponent is the Altos.

936
00:47:48,399 --> 00:47:50,633
How do you think the game will go, Su Bin?

937
00:47:51,502 --> 00:47:52,836
It won't be easy...

938
00:47:53,204 --> 00:47:54,571
- It won't be easy?
- No.

939
00:47:56,007 --> 00:47:59,042
What are the weaknesses of the Altos?

940
00:47:59,477 --> 00:48:01,411
Their side blocks are a bit low.

941
00:48:01,412 --> 00:48:02,412
Their side blocks are a bit low,

942
00:48:02,713 --> 00:48:04,248
especially the blocks from position two.

943
00:48:04,272 --> 00:48:06,272
(The Altos' blocks
from position two are low.)

944
00:48:06,450 --> 00:48:08,117
Then, where should we aim when attacking?

945
00:48:08,119 --> 00:48:09,252
(Then, what's our strategy?)

946
00:48:09,620 --> 00:48:11,521
(Target the opponent's weak spot
at position two!)

947
00:48:12,590 --> 00:48:15,659
(When the setter sets to the left,)

948
00:48:16,553 --> 00:48:20,596
(the outside hitter on the left should
focus attacks on position two.)

949
00:48:20,598 --> 00:48:24,434
I thought it would be difficult
to break through the opponent...

950
00:48:24,435 --> 00:48:27,704
using only our existing attacking options.

951
00:48:27,705 --> 00:48:32,409
So we plan to attack
from different angles and positions...

952
00:48:32,410 --> 00:48:35,279
to disrupt their blocking
and defensive line.

953
00:48:35,279 --> 00:48:37,079
If not, our plays may become unstable.

954
00:48:37,312 --> 00:48:39,679
So setters are really important.

955
00:48:41,212 --> 00:48:43,246
(Training for the match
against the Altos begins)

956
00:48:43,979 --> 00:48:47,112
(Our target is the opponents' zone 2.)

957
00:48:47,712 --> 00:48:50,279
(The setter must set the ball
to the left.)

958
00:48:52,746 --> 00:48:55,512
(Setter Lee Na-Yeon sets it to the right.)

959
00:48:57,646 --> 00:48:59,279
Why did you toss it to the right?
It should be left.

960
00:49:01,679 --> 00:49:03,812
(Unlike their strategy,)

961
00:49:03,812 --> 00:49:06,312
(the setters toss the ball
to the right only.)

962
00:49:07,312 --> 00:49:08,646
What's wrong with you, setters?

963
00:49:10,179 --> 00:49:11,179
Hey.

964
00:49:11,679 --> 00:49:13,212
Did you forget the success rate?

965
00:49:13,712 --> 00:49:14,879
We've decided what to do.

966
00:49:16,046 --> 00:49:17,312
You already know about low blocks.

967
00:49:17,679 --> 00:49:19,846
Set the ball without mercy!

968
00:49:20,079 --> 00:49:21,379
Then what should the hitters do?

969
00:49:21,646 --> 00:49:23,612
Attack there relentlessly!

970
00:49:23,779 --> 00:49:25,746
They must think,
"That team is going too far."

971
00:49:25,946 --> 00:49:28,912
Keep hitting their weak spots!
Did you get it?

972
00:49:29,079 --> 00:49:33,012
They have a weakness.
It's our chance, so keep attacking it.

973
00:49:33,012 --> 00:49:34,912
- Until they think we're merciless. Okay?
- Yes, Coach.

974
00:49:38,279 --> 00:49:40,312
Hit it with no mercy!

975
00:49:41,812 --> 00:49:43,112
(The ball goes to the back.)

976
00:49:43,446 --> 00:49:45,746
Why did you set it to her
with a back attack?

977
00:49:46,046 --> 00:49:47,979
Memorize it! This is frustrating me.

978
00:49:48,079 --> 00:49:49,879
Sol, it's too high.

979
00:49:49,912 --> 00:49:51,646
Eyes to your side, Jin.

980
00:49:51,646 --> 00:49:53,479
Na-Yeon, catch it properly.

981
00:49:53,512 --> 00:49:56,479
Why are you exhausted?
You're not even 30 yet!

982
00:49:57,746 --> 00:49:58,746
You're over 30?

983
00:49:59,079 --> 00:50:00,512
- Not yet.
- You're not 30 yet, right?

984
00:50:01,179 --> 00:50:03,046
I knew it. Why are you tired then?

985
00:50:03,612 --> 00:50:06,112
I told you you should set it like this!

986
00:50:06,112 --> 00:50:07,112
Set it harder!

987
00:50:07,112 --> 00:50:08,446
Higher, Na-Yeon.

988
00:50:08,446 --> 00:50:13,546
(Their strategy begins
to sink in gradually.)

989
00:50:13,746 --> 00:50:16,512
(The team improves
with Coach Kim's constant yells.)

990
00:50:18,012 --> 00:50:20,612
(Their big match is
just around the corner.)

991
00:50:22,179 --> 00:50:25,746
(Wake up every muscle!)

992
00:50:26,379 --> 00:50:29,712
(Protein time after exercise)

993
00:50:30,479 --> 00:50:32,146
(Choosing their flavor)

994
00:50:32,579 --> 00:50:34,479
(Ending the session with a protein drink)

995
00:50:34,512 --> 00:50:36,379
This has no sugar,
but it's still delicious.

996
00:50:36,379 --> 00:50:37,812
This protein drink is so good.

997
00:50:38,312 --> 00:50:40,012
(D-1 at last)

998
00:50:40,146 --> 00:50:43,012
Did you sleep well?
Today's training will be so simple.

999
00:50:43,312 --> 00:50:45,846
Our target serving speed is 65km/h.
Each of you must do it seven times.

1000
00:50:45,846 --> 00:50:47,279
And your training will be over.

1001
00:50:47,279 --> 00:50:49,412
- Yes.
- Alright. You may start.

1002
00:50:49,646 --> 00:50:51,046
(The key point
of the serving training is...)

1003
00:50:51,279 --> 00:50:53,646
(a speed gun.)

1004
00:50:53,779 --> 00:50:56,212
(It is to measure the speed accurately.)

1005
00:50:57,246 --> 00:50:58,246
It's 69!

1006
00:50:59,179 --> 00:51:00,746
(Enkhsoyol serves.)

1007
00:51:00,779 --> 00:51:01,779
That's it!

1008
00:51:01,946 --> 00:51:02,946
It's 84!

1009
00:51:02,946 --> 00:51:05,012
(Enkhsoyol's speed is 84km/h.)

1010
00:51:05,012 --> 00:51:06,879
(Meanwhile, for Myoung-Hwa)

1011
00:51:06,879 --> 00:51:07,879
It's 33.

1012
00:51:09,279 --> 00:51:11,012
Let's go home, Myoung-Hwa!

1013
00:51:11,779 --> 00:51:14,912
(Myoung-Hwa is the only one left
on the court.)

1014
00:51:16,512 --> 00:51:17,512
It's 64!

1015
00:51:19,712 --> 00:51:21,246
Come on, Myoung-Hwa! You got this.

1016
00:51:22,512 --> 00:51:26,479
Myoung-Hwa, you need to use power
the moment you hit the ball.

1017
00:51:27,746 --> 00:51:29,112
(She tries again after listening
to Coach Kim's advice.)

1018
00:51:29,112 --> 00:51:30,112
It's 61.

1019
00:51:31,346 --> 00:51:33,246
- That was fast.
- It's 61.

1020
00:51:35,146 --> 00:51:36,146
It's 61.

1021
00:51:37,446 --> 00:51:40,146
(Her teammates wait outside the court.)

1022
00:51:46,479 --> 00:51:47,479
It's 62.

1023
00:51:48,879 --> 00:51:50,446
- What's the speed?
- It's 62!

1024
00:51:52,179 --> 00:51:53,546
Wrap up now.

1025
00:51:53,546 --> 00:51:55,279
- Thank you for your hard work.
- You did well.

1026
00:51:55,779 --> 00:51:57,012
It hurts so much.

1027
00:51:57,012 --> 00:52:00,079
Haven't you ever practiced serving
with a speed gun?

1028
00:52:00,079 --> 00:52:02,412
No, I haven't.

1029
00:52:02,412 --> 00:52:04,012
Then what do you practice with?

1030
00:52:04,279 --> 00:52:05,379
Nothing.

1031
00:52:05,379 --> 00:52:06,379
You just serve?

1032
00:52:10,412 --> 00:52:13,846
Why are you crying, Myoung-Hwa?
This is too sudden.

1033
00:52:14,646 --> 00:52:16,812
She tried really hard.

1034
00:52:17,546 --> 00:52:19,846
Myoung-Hwa is crying. Put the cameras in.

1035
00:52:20,346 --> 00:52:21,946
Coach!

1036
00:52:22,179 --> 00:52:23,179
She's crying.

1037
00:52:23,179 --> 00:52:24,579
(Covering her)

1038
00:52:24,679 --> 00:52:26,179
You did your best.

1039
00:52:31,046 --> 00:52:33,879
After I injured my shoulder,

1040
00:52:34,279 --> 00:52:35,712
I haven't served much.

1041
00:52:35,979 --> 00:52:39,146
I felt humiliated for not hitting 65km/h.

1042
00:52:39,346 --> 00:52:42,946
My shoulder also hurt a lot,
so I guess I had mixed feelings.

1043
00:52:43,546 --> 00:52:44,846
You all did great today.

1044
00:52:45,546 --> 00:52:49,012
Now, I know why head coaches always say
they lack time.

1045
00:52:49,412 --> 00:52:50,879
I want one more session.

1046
00:52:51,512 --> 00:52:52,912
But we'll end the training today.

1047
00:52:53,146 --> 00:52:56,279
We received a notice from the Altos.

1048
00:52:56,879 --> 00:52:58,879
It's a list of their players.

1049
00:52:59,312 --> 00:53:01,646
Kim Chae Won will go.

1050
00:53:02,046 --> 00:53:03,646
There's Kim Ha Kyung.

1051
00:53:03,646 --> 00:53:05,779
And they also have Hwang Min Kyoung.

1052
00:53:06,046 --> 00:53:07,112
They're all coming.

1053
00:53:07,112 --> 00:53:09,346
Lee So Young will join as well.

1054
00:53:09,979 --> 00:53:10,979
Everyone is coming then.

1055
00:53:10,979 --> 00:53:12,046
(They added players to fill gaps.)

1056
00:53:12,046 --> 00:53:14,712
I don't know if they were afraid of us,

1057
00:53:15,212 --> 00:53:18,412
but they added
four starting-caliber players.

1058
00:53:19,446 --> 00:53:23,412
I think they were concerned
that they might lose to us.

1059
00:53:26,546 --> 00:53:28,879
(In Wonder Dogs' home stadium,)

1060
00:53:29,679 --> 00:53:32,712
(the first match
with the pro team will begin.)

1061
00:53:37,579 --> 00:53:40,979
(The opposing team's bus enters
Wonder Dogs' stadium.)

1062
00:53:48,779 --> 00:53:52,246
(Kim Ha Kyung, setter)

1063
00:53:54,379 --> 00:53:57,646
(Hwang Min Kyoung, outside hitter)

1064
00:53:58,646 --> 00:54:02,112
(Lee So Young, outside hitter)

1065
00:54:02,746 --> 00:54:06,612
(Their elite coaching staff is
followed by...)

1066
00:54:08,212 --> 00:54:11,679
(Head Coach Kim Ho Chul)

1067
00:54:12,212 --> 00:54:14,812
(The Altos head coach
and coaching staff waiting room)

1068
00:54:14,846 --> 00:54:18,912
- Hello.
- Nice to meet you.

1069
00:54:19,612 --> 00:54:20,612
Welcome.

1070
00:54:21,079 --> 00:54:23,012
- It's been a long time.
- Yes.

1071
00:54:23,479 --> 00:54:25,479
- I can't believe we're meeting here.
- I know, right?

1072
00:54:26,446 --> 00:54:28,712
We heard there's a huge cheering squad
for your team today.

1073
00:54:28,846 --> 00:54:32,779
It's our company's founding anniversary.

1074
00:54:33,079 --> 00:54:37,012
So they must have been invited
to celebrate.

1075
00:54:38,112 --> 00:54:39,179
(Clappers)

1076
00:54:39,912 --> 00:54:41,179
(Cheerleaders)

1077
00:54:41,679 --> 00:54:43,412
(Uniforms)

1078
00:54:45,246 --> 00:54:48,979
(They're as enormous as in the V-League.)

1079
00:54:49,712 --> 00:54:51,712
Why did you stack
up your lineup like that?

1080
00:54:52,079 --> 00:54:53,112
- Our lineup?
- Yes.

1081
00:54:53,112 --> 00:54:54,946
Even Lee So Young
and Hwang Min Kyoung are there.

1082
00:54:54,979 --> 00:54:58,079
- They are on the list.
- Are they not playing?

1083
00:54:58,246 --> 00:54:59,379
Of course they are.

1084
00:55:01,112 --> 00:55:03,846
We don't have other players
for their positions.

1085
00:55:04,479 --> 00:55:06,679
Team Yeon Koung has nothing to lose...

1086
00:55:07,712 --> 00:55:09,012
when they compete with a pro team.

1087
00:55:09,012 --> 00:55:11,312
They will be fine
whether they win or lose.

1088
00:55:11,379 --> 00:55:13,779
For us, winning is expected.

1089
00:55:14,812 --> 00:55:16,546
But if we lose, it's a huge embarrassment.

1090
00:55:16,912 --> 00:55:17,912
Am I wrong?

1091
00:55:17,912 --> 00:55:19,279
So you'll give it all you've got.

1092
00:55:20,912 --> 00:55:23,646
(A professional coach's resolute mindset)

1093
00:55:23,946 --> 00:55:26,779
Wonder Dogs also have
many players from the Altos.

1094
00:55:27,312 --> 00:55:29,979
I don't understand why there are a lot.

1095
00:55:30,279 --> 00:55:31,646
They're all ready to fight.

1096
00:55:33,346 --> 00:55:34,879
Are they fired up because of me?

1097
00:55:36,479 --> 00:55:38,412
(One of the fired up ones)

1098
00:55:39,346 --> 00:55:41,779
- Hello.
- Hi.

1099
00:55:41,946 --> 00:55:46,346
- Great to see you.
- Hello.

1100
00:55:46,379 --> 00:55:48,212
You look so happy
after winning your first game.

1101
00:55:48,212 --> 00:55:50,379
(Commentators immediately visit
the Wonder Dogs' coaching staff.)

1102
00:55:51,212 --> 00:55:52,412
What was it like after your first game?

1103
00:55:52,579 --> 00:55:53,579
After the first game?

1104
00:55:54,112 --> 00:55:55,779
We had many errors.

1105
00:55:56,246 --> 00:55:59,179
So we had to review them.

1106
00:56:00,646 --> 00:56:03,479
Your eyes look so tired.

1107
00:56:03,612 --> 00:56:05,179
This is not an easy task to do.

1108
00:56:06,146 --> 00:56:08,184
(Trembling)

1109
00:56:10,212 --> 00:56:12,612
It's way different from just chatting
during the match.

1110
00:56:13,946 --> 00:56:15,412
It's not the same at all.

1111
00:56:15,546 --> 00:56:18,746
I'm starting to understand
how leaders feel.

1112
00:56:19,079 --> 00:56:21,879
Why do you keep entering the court?
You shouldn't do that.

1113
00:56:22,246 --> 00:56:24,012
You were way inside the court.

1114
00:56:25,179 --> 00:56:27,946
(During their first game,)

1115
00:56:28,646 --> 00:56:31,112
(Coach Kim was in the court
all of a sudden.)

1116
00:56:31,146 --> 00:56:33,612
(About to join as a player)

1117
00:56:36,046 --> 00:56:37,479
Well, they didn't warn me.

1118
00:56:38,946 --> 00:56:41,646
It's your first match with a pro team.

1119
00:56:41,779 --> 00:56:44,446
Is Pyo Seung Ju okay today?

1120
00:56:45,379 --> 00:56:48,512
(Due to a tear in her calf muscle,)

1121
00:56:49,246 --> 00:56:52,512
(Seung Ju, the ace of the team...)

1122
00:56:52,512 --> 00:56:55,879
(couldn't play in the first game.)

1123
00:56:56,212 --> 00:56:57,479
Is she in the starting lineup today?

1124
00:56:57,479 --> 00:56:59,079
- Who?
- Pyo Seung Ju.

1125
00:56:59,412 --> 00:57:00,579
I believe she will.

1126
00:57:02,112 --> 00:57:04,146
She has recovered well from her injury.

1127
00:57:04,912 --> 00:57:06,712
Although she's not fully healed,

1128
00:57:06,912 --> 00:57:10,446
we decided to defeat the Altos
even if it may be a little risky.

1129
00:57:10,712 --> 00:57:12,279
You also have a history with the Altos.

1130
00:57:15,212 --> 00:57:16,246
Maybe even today?

1131
00:57:16,246 --> 00:57:18,379
We don't know what will happen.

1132
00:57:18,612 --> 00:57:20,712
The match might get intense.

1133
00:57:21,579 --> 00:57:24,146
(Expectation...)

1134
00:57:24,146 --> 00:57:26,579
(becomes reality?)

1135
00:57:27,046 --> 00:57:29,546
(It's a battle between head coaches,)

1136
00:57:29,979 --> 00:57:33,579
(where neither can back down.)

1137
00:57:33,946 --> 00:57:36,246
(Kim Ho Chul vs. Kim Yeon Koung)

1138
00:57:36,746 --> 00:57:42,212
(The war between head coaches will
soon begin.)

1139
00:57:42,212 --> 00:57:44,679
Hi, guys.

1140
00:57:45,579 --> 00:57:46,979
Are you guys ready?

1141
00:57:48,312 --> 00:57:49,245
Are you feeling okay?

1142
00:57:50,679 --> 00:57:53,012
Come on. How are you guys feeling?

1143
00:57:53,012 --> 00:57:55,279
Hye In and Jin, you guys look so tense.

1144
00:57:56,679 --> 00:57:58,279
- You're okay, right?
- Yes.

1145
00:57:58,845 --> 00:58:00,845
Today's starting lineup is...

1146
00:58:01,837 --> 00:58:04,674
(Outside hitters)

1147
00:58:05,322 --> 00:58:07,555
Seung Ju and Enkhsoyol.

1148
00:58:09,188 --> 00:58:11,622
Na Hee and Hyeon Jeong are
the middle blockers.

1149
00:58:11,955 --> 00:58:14,388
(Middle blockers, Na Hee and Hyeon Jeong)

1150
00:58:14,522 --> 00:58:16,188
Young In and Hye In.

1151
00:58:16,188 --> 00:58:18,488
(Opposite hitters, Young In and Hye In)

1152
00:58:18,855 --> 00:58:19,822
And then...

1153
00:58:19,822 --> 00:58:22,755
(Who's going to be the last setter?)

1154
00:58:23,055 --> 00:58:25,388
And then Jin.

1155
00:58:25,388 --> 00:58:26,688
These are starting members,

1156
00:58:26,688 --> 00:58:28,022
so get ready.

1157
00:58:28,022 --> 00:58:29,288
- Got it?
- Yes, coach.

1158
00:58:30,288 --> 00:58:33,488
I'm going to show them what I can do...

1159
00:58:33,488 --> 00:58:34,588
once I'm on that court.

1160
00:58:34,588 --> 00:58:36,788
I think we have a good chance of winning.

1161
00:58:37,188 --> 00:58:39,955
All I can think about is
how badly I want to win.

1162
00:58:40,355 --> 00:58:43,422
I just really want to win.

1163
00:58:44,655 --> 00:58:46,822
(Going towards a winning streak)

1164
00:58:47,122 --> 00:58:50,455
Wonder Dogs have tasted sweet victory
in their first game,

1165
00:58:50,455 --> 00:58:51,988
and now they're up for their second match.

1166
00:58:51,988 --> 00:58:53,188
Please stay tuned.

1167
00:58:53,188 --> 00:58:54,655
- Hello.
- Hello.

1168
00:58:54,655 --> 00:58:57,655
Wonder Dogs won their first game
with great spirits.

1169
00:58:57,655 --> 00:59:01,988
But their next opponent is way too strong,
even considering they won the last one.

1170
00:59:01,988 --> 00:59:02,788
They're a pro team.

1171
00:59:02,788 --> 00:59:05,522
Their first opponent was
a high school champion,

1172
00:59:05,522 --> 00:59:09,122
but a pro team and a high school team are
completely different.

1173
00:59:09,122 --> 00:59:11,022
Today, Pilseung Wonder Dogs are
up against...

1174
00:59:11,022 --> 00:59:12,755
a pro team, the Altos.

1175
00:59:12,755 --> 00:59:15,555
(The Altos players are
entering the court.)

1176
00:59:23,355 --> 00:59:24,888
Hey, what are you doing here?

1177
00:59:24,888 --> 00:59:26,188
- I'm retired now.
- What?

1178
00:59:26,188 --> 00:59:28,188
- I'm retired.
- You are?

1179
00:59:30,988 --> 00:59:33,622
Oh, dear. Everyone's here.

1180
00:59:33,822 --> 00:59:35,355
(A 30-year veteran coach)

1181
00:59:35,355 --> 00:59:36,388
(Today's line referee)

1182
00:59:36,622 --> 00:59:37,555
Oh, hey.

1183
00:59:37,555 --> 00:59:40,388
(Endless greetings all around)

1184
00:59:41,888 --> 00:59:43,988
- They have a big team.
- Yes.

1185
00:59:44,855 --> 00:59:47,622
(Players from both teams saying
hello to each other)

1186
00:59:47,755 --> 00:59:49,788
How come you're wearing
a blue and orange uniform?

1187
00:59:49,788 --> 00:59:51,988
You joined their team now?
You seem taller somehow.

1188
00:59:52,355 --> 00:59:54,455
Seung Ju didn't get to play last time,

1189
00:59:54,455 --> 00:59:57,022
so this is her first game
after her retirement.

1190
00:59:57,022 --> 00:59:57,855
That's right.

1191
00:59:57,855 --> 00:59:59,588
Seung Ju used to play for the Altos,

1192
00:59:59,588 --> 01:00:02,588
but you could say that
when So Young joined the Altos,

1193
01:00:02,588 --> 01:00:04,755
she was left
off the protected player list...

1194
01:00:04,755 --> 01:00:06,622
- and transferred to the Red Sparks.
- That's correct.

1195
01:00:06,622 --> 01:00:07,822
She could even think that...

1196
01:00:07,822 --> 01:00:09,955
- They didn't hold on to her.
- That's right.

1197
01:00:09,955 --> 01:00:10,855
Yes.

1198
01:00:10,855 --> 01:00:12,022
"I'll show you."

1199
01:00:12,022 --> 01:00:14,088
She could definitely be feeling that way.

1200
01:00:14,088 --> 01:00:15,388
I guess so.

1201
01:00:15,388 --> 01:00:16,455
I'm an underdog now.

1202
01:00:16,455 --> 01:00:17,755
I'm teamless.

1203
01:00:17,755 --> 01:00:18,722
I'm an underdog.

1204
01:00:19,222 --> 01:00:21,155
- Hey, there.
- Hi.

1205
01:00:21,155 --> 01:00:22,422
It's been so long.

1206
01:00:22,422 --> 01:00:24,355
Have we ever been
on the same team together?

1207
01:00:24,355 --> 01:00:26,422
- Yes, we have.
- Right?

1208
01:00:26,422 --> 01:00:27,522
It's been so long.

1209
01:00:27,522 --> 01:00:29,055
We haven't seen each other for so long.

1210
01:00:29,522 --> 01:00:32,388
I have high expectations for Jin today.

1211
01:00:32,388 --> 01:00:35,388
Yes, Coach Kim Ho Chul is known
as a legendary setter.

1212
01:00:35,388 --> 01:00:38,222
- He was even called a computer setter.
- That's right.

1213
01:00:38,655 --> 01:00:42,255
(Coach Ho Chul places
great importance on setters,)

1214
01:00:42,688 --> 01:00:46,855
(and Ha Kyung and Jin were his protégés.)

1215
01:00:46,855 --> 01:00:49,122
He even had a setter school called
the Ho Chul School,

1216
01:00:49,122 --> 01:00:52,288
and Jin was
one of the players trained there.

1217
01:00:52,288 --> 01:00:55,122
But she was released from the team,
and this is her first game since then.

1218
01:00:55,122 --> 01:00:58,122
- I'm hoping for a dramatic game today.
- Yes, me too.

1219
01:00:58,688 --> 01:00:59,688
Are you guys good?
- You mean us?
- Yes.

1220
01:01:01,522 --> 01:01:02,588
Do you practice every day?

1221
01:01:02,588 --> 01:01:04,122
- We're so exhausted.
- You practice every day?

1222
01:01:04,122 --> 01:01:04,988
Of course.
But we do rest too.

1223
01:01:05,822 --> 01:01:07,822
Oh, my. What if we lose today?

1224
01:01:07,822 --> 01:01:10,055
You guys are a professional team.

1225
01:01:10,055 --> 01:01:12,855
You guys are all professional players too.

1226
01:01:12,855 --> 01:01:14,755
I've been teamless for a year.

1227
01:01:15,288 --> 01:01:17,188
I have to win this game.

1228
01:01:17,588 --> 01:01:20,555
I need to win this setter battle,
at least.

1229
01:01:20,555 --> 01:01:22,622
I just want to win so bad.

1230
01:01:23,422 --> 01:01:24,455
Are you guys good?

1231
01:01:25,688 --> 01:01:26,855
Have you played?

1232
01:01:27,288 --> 01:01:28,222
Against other teams?

1233
01:01:28,588 --> 01:01:29,388
(Keeping silent)

1234
01:01:29,388 --> 01:01:30,755
Hey, take it easy on us.

1235
01:01:30,755 --> 01:01:31,988
You go easy on us too.

1236
01:01:31,988 --> 01:01:34,055
Seriously. Go easy on us.

1237
01:01:34,055 --> 01:01:35,322
Hello.

1238
01:01:35,322 --> 01:01:36,388
Is he here?

1239
01:01:36,388 --> 01:01:38,388
Let's go say hi to the coach.

1240
01:01:38,388 --> 01:01:39,388
- Hello.
- Hi.

1241
01:01:39,622 --> 01:01:41,922
- Hi, coach.
- Hello, coach.

1242
01:01:41,922 --> 01:01:43,422
- You're here too, General?
- Yes.

1243
01:01:43,422 --> 01:01:45,622
- You didn't know?
- I didn't.

1244
01:01:45,622 --> 01:01:46,922
How have you been, coach?

1245
01:01:46,922 --> 01:01:48,655
- You're here too, Jin?
- Yes.

1246
01:01:48,655 --> 01:01:49,755
And Hye In too.

1247
01:01:49,755 --> 01:01:50,722
Hello.

1248
01:01:51,455 --> 01:01:53,255
- Is your back better now?
- It is.

1249
01:01:53,255 --> 01:01:54,788
(They all used to play on his team.)

1250
01:02:04,022 --> 01:02:06,588
- Good luck.
- You too, coach.

1251
01:02:23,255 --> 01:02:26,188
- Hello. Hi.
- Hey.

1252
01:02:26,188 --> 01:02:27,888
- Nice to see you, coach.
- It's all a bit sudden.

1253
01:02:28,588 --> 01:02:32,288
Coach Yeon Koung
and Coach Ho Chul are saying hello.

1254
01:02:32,288 --> 01:02:35,622
- They've met each other in the V-League.
- Multiple times on court.

1255
01:02:35,622 --> 01:02:37,222
They were very enthusiastic.

1256
01:02:37,222 --> 01:02:41,088
They shared a lot of intense moments
on the court and on the sidelines.

1257
01:02:41,088 --> 01:02:45,155
But Coach Yeon Koung said she's going
to put all that history aside...

1258
01:02:45,155 --> 01:02:47,355
- and just do her thing.
- That's right.

1259
01:02:47,655 --> 01:02:49,155
Do you think she'll be able to do that?

1260
01:02:49,155 --> 01:02:53,922
I believe she was only able to say that
because the game hasn't started.

1261
01:02:53,922 --> 01:02:55,188
Once the game starts,

1262
01:02:55,188 --> 01:02:57,855
you never know how things will turn out.

1263
01:02:57,855 --> 01:03:01,122
We can all agree that Coach Yeon Koung was
one of the best players.

1264
01:03:01,122 --> 01:03:04,288
Meanwhile, Coach Ho Chul
of the opposing team...

1265
01:03:04,288 --> 01:03:07,455
was not only a remarkable player...

1266
01:03:07,455 --> 01:03:10,655
but he's also a veteran coach
with 30 years of experience.

1267
01:03:10,655 --> 01:03:13,488
Since he's up against a rookie coach,

1268
01:03:13,488 --> 01:03:16,088
I'm sure he's somewhat confident
in the battle of strategies.

1269
01:03:16,088 --> 01:03:18,288
- Go easy on us, coach.
- Oh, yes?

1270
01:03:18,288 --> 01:03:19,255
Why go easy on you?

1271
01:03:19,255 --> 01:03:20,588
You've got great players on your team.

1272
01:03:21,255 --> 01:03:22,122
What?

1273
01:03:22,122 --> 01:03:24,288
Still, what's with the emergency call-up?

1274
01:03:24,722 --> 01:03:27,488
No, I'll decide later how to play this.

1275
01:03:27,488 --> 01:03:29,855
You can't just bring
in all your star players like that!

1276
01:03:29,855 --> 01:03:33,455
You've got Min Kyoung, So Young,
Ha Kyung, and Chae Won.

1277
01:03:33,455 --> 01:03:35,555
- I won't put them all in.
- You won't?

1278
01:03:35,555 --> 01:03:37,822
We'll see how it goes and substitute.

1279
01:03:37,822 --> 01:03:39,655
- All right. Go easy.
- Okay.

1280
01:03:39,655 --> 01:03:41,555
Good luck, coach.

1281
01:03:41,555 --> 01:03:42,488
Good luck.

1282
01:03:50,688 --> 01:03:51,655
So let's see.

1283
01:03:52,355 --> 01:03:54,322
Should we put Jeong Min and Ha Kyung in?

1284
01:03:54,922 --> 01:03:56,988
(Middle blocker, Choi Jeong Min)

1285
01:03:57,288 --> 01:03:59,122
(Setter, Kim Ha Kyung)

1286
01:03:59,622 --> 01:04:02,055
(Starting lineup decided)

1287
01:04:02,488 --> 01:04:05,655
All right, let's talk about today's lineup
for Wonder Dogs.

1288
01:04:05,655 --> 01:04:07,888
First off, we have Kim Hyeon Jeong
as middle blocker,

1289
01:04:07,888 --> 01:04:09,622
and Yoon Young In as opposite hitter.

1290
01:04:09,622 --> 01:04:11,055
Enkhsoyol as outside hitter.

1291
01:04:11,055 --> 01:04:12,455
Kim Na Hee as middle blocker.

1292
01:04:12,455 --> 01:04:13,822
Lee Jin as setter.

1293
01:04:13,822 --> 01:04:15,288
Pyo Seung Ju as outside hitter.

1294
01:04:15,288 --> 01:04:16,822
Koo Hye In as libero.

1295
01:04:16,822 --> 01:04:19,155
Now, let's look at the Altos' lineup.

1296
01:04:19,155 --> 01:04:20,455
Kim Ha Kyung as setter.

1297
01:04:20,455 --> 01:04:22,055
Go Ui Jeong as outside hitter.

1298
01:04:22,055 --> 01:04:23,588
Kim Chae Yeon as middle blocker.

1299
01:04:23,588 --> 01:04:25,088
Jeon Su Min as opposite hitter.

1300
01:04:25,088 --> 01:04:26,855
Hwang Min Kyoung as outside hitter.

1301
01:04:26,855 --> 01:04:28,322
Choi Jeong Min as middle blocker.

1302
01:04:28,322 --> 01:04:29,855
Kim Chae Won as libero.

1303
01:04:29,855 --> 01:04:32,588
Four of them were
in the starting lineup last season.

1304
01:04:32,588 --> 01:04:33,555
That's right.

1305
01:04:33,555 --> 01:04:37,055
Libero, outside hitter,
middle, and setter.

1306
01:04:37,055 --> 01:04:40,788
You can even say that setter
and libero are the key players in a game,

1307
01:04:40,788 --> 01:04:44,655
and they put in the players
who were in the main lineup last year.

1308
01:04:44,655 --> 01:04:47,255
It's a David and Goliath matchup here.

1309
01:04:47,255 --> 01:04:50,888
But if Wonder Dogs can
overcome these challenges,

1310
01:04:50,888 --> 01:04:53,788
- I believe the players will grow.
- That's right.

1311
01:04:55,255 --> 01:04:59,655
(Coach Tae Young has obtained
the opponent lineup.)

1312
01:05:00,355 --> 01:05:01,288
Who's at opposite hitter?

1313
01:05:01,755 --> 01:05:02,788
Jeon Su Min.

1314
01:05:03,455 --> 01:05:04,955
Player number 22, in zone one.

1315
01:05:04,955 --> 01:05:06,388
- Su Min on the right?
- That's correct.

1316
01:05:06,388 --> 01:05:08,922
And then who? Go Ui Jeong?

1317
01:05:10,322 --> 01:05:14,088
(Her strategy was based on Su Min
playing as an outside hitter.)

1318
01:05:14,288 --> 01:05:15,355
Gather up, guys.

1319
01:05:16,488 --> 01:05:19,088
There's a slight change in plan.

1320
01:05:19,688 --> 01:05:22,622
Jeon Su Min is going to play at the right,

1321
01:05:22,622 --> 01:05:24,988
and Min Kyoung will play on the left
with Ui Jeong.

1322
01:05:24,988 --> 01:05:28,155
- But we're sticking to our plan.
- Okay.

1323
01:05:28,155 --> 01:05:30,555
Don't worry.
Just stick to what we've prepared.

1324
01:05:30,555 --> 01:05:31,355
Let's go!

1325
01:05:31,355 --> 01:05:33,755
- Let's get it!
- Let's go!

1326
01:05:33,755 --> 01:05:36,455
- Pilseung Wonder Dogs!
- Wonder Dogs!

1327
01:05:39,588 --> 01:05:42,155
Listen up, everyone.

1328
01:05:42,888 --> 01:05:44,488
Some of the opposing players are rookies,

1329
01:05:45,022 --> 01:05:46,588
but some have played volleyball
for a long time,

1330
01:05:46,588 --> 01:05:48,788
which means they're experienced.

1331
01:05:48,788 --> 01:05:52,588
If we stay passive,
we could be in trouble.

1332
01:05:52,588 --> 01:05:53,688
So let's not sit back.

1333
01:05:53,688 --> 01:05:55,255
They've been practicing a lot,

1334
01:05:55,255 --> 01:05:57,488
but there will probably be
more unorthodox plays...

1335
01:05:57,488 --> 01:05:59,622
rather than standard attacks.

1336
01:05:59,622 --> 01:06:03,122
If that happens,
we can bring the defense line up front.

1337
01:06:03,122 --> 01:06:04,655
Keep that in mind, got it?

1338
01:06:04,655 --> 01:06:05,588
- Yes, coach.
- Yes, coach.

1339
01:06:06,988 --> 01:06:09,588
- Let's go, Altos!
- Let's go, Altos!

1340
01:06:13,355 --> 01:06:20,122
- Clap it up for the Altos!
- Clap it up for the Altos!

1341
01:06:20,588 --> 01:06:22,988
(As the game is about to begin,)

1342
01:06:23,688 --> 01:06:26,655
(the cheer captain starts
to lead the crowd with team chants.)

1343
01:06:31,622 --> 01:06:34,455
(Wonder Dogs' families are sitting
on the opposite side.)

1344
01:06:34,888 --> 01:06:37,188
(Hye In's aunt, grandmother, and brother)

1345
01:06:37,722 --> 01:06:39,755
(Na-Yeon's husband and father)

1346
01:06:40,188 --> 01:06:42,488
(Seung Ju's husband and in-laws)

1347
01:06:43,022 --> 01:06:45,588
(Jin's father)

1348
01:06:45,922 --> 01:06:48,255
I feel like we should at least get
matching team shirts too.

1349
01:06:49,722 --> 01:06:51,855
- We should get team shirts too.
- Such a big group of fans.

1350
01:06:52,022 --> 01:06:54,322
We should crush them
when their cheering squad's that big.

1351
01:06:54,322 --> 01:06:55,755
Darn it.

1352
01:06:56,388 --> 01:06:58,788
Wonder Dogs' second game.

1353
01:06:58,788 --> 01:07:00,322
They're up against the Altos.

1354
01:07:00,322 --> 01:07:03,455
It's their first match against a pro team.

1355
01:07:04,322 --> 01:07:07,388
(A pro team...)

1356
01:07:07,388 --> 01:07:10,822
(and underdogs)

1357
01:07:10,822 --> 01:07:13,055
(A setter that was released
from a pro team)

1358
01:07:13,055 --> 01:07:16,755
(against a current pro team setter)

1359
01:07:16,755 --> 01:07:20,122
(Pro team hitters...)

1360
01:07:20,122 --> 01:07:21,055
(and pro coach...)
(against a rookie coach)

1361
01:07:24,588 --> 01:07:28,055
(They'll either crush them or be crushed.)

1362
01:07:28,188 --> 01:07:30,255
Let's kick off the match with the Altos.

1363
01:07:31,248 --> 01:07:34,014
Hyeon Jeong's serve kicks off...

1364
01:07:34,014 --> 01:07:35,048
the first set!

1365
01:07:37,988 --> 01:07:38,888
Ha Kyung.

1366
01:07:39,221 --> 01:07:40,588
(It's a back toss.)

1367
01:07:40,588 --> 01:07:41,621
Feint!

1368
01:07:43,021 --> 01:07:45,821
(Feinting the blocker
and consecutive attacks)

1369
01:07:46,988 --> 01:07:47,955
It's a super save!

1370
01:07:52,288 --> 01:07:53,488
It's Chae Yeon again.

1371
01:07:54,221 --> 01:07:55,288
(This time, a front toss)

1372
01:07:55,288 --> 01:07:56,555
Spike!

1373
01:07:57,655 --> 01:08:00,455
(A perfect set leads
to a successful spike.)

1374
01:08:03,988 --> 01:08:05,455
Great job.

1375
01:08:07,088 --> 01:08:09,655
It's Su Min.

1376
01:08:09,655 --> 01:08:12,455
She's a player with considerable power.

1377
01:08:12,455 --> 01:08:15,755
She joined the league...

1378
01:08:15,755 --> 01:08:18,121
as the third pick in the first round
of the 2013-2014 season.

1379
01:08:18,121 --> 01:08:21,321
The Altos take the first point.

1380
01:08:21,988 --> 01:08:24,588
Focus on defense.
Position yourself for defense.

1381
01:08:26,955 --> 01:08:28,021
Jin.

1382
01:08:28,021 --> 01:08:31,121
- Watch it and join them.
- Okay.

1383
01:08:31,121 --> 01:08:32,288
It's 1 to 0.

1384
01:08:33,855 --> 01:08:35,555
It's a serve by Ui Jeong of the Altos.

1385
01:08:35,555 --> 01:08:37,388
- She has an excellent serve.
- Absolutely.

1386
01:08:37,388 --> 01:08:39,255
Her serve is one of her strengths.

1387
01:08:39,888 --> 01:08:41,959
Keep moving. Her serve is off right now.

1388
01:08:42,821 --> 01:08:44,055
Give a signal to each other.

1389
01:08:49,388 --> 01:08:51,288
Break it!

1390
01:08:53,688 --> 01:08:55,688
(Hesitating)

1391
01:08:57,088 --> 01:08:58,488
Jin, move quickly.

1392
01:08:59,455 --> 01:09:00,421
Seung Ju set it,

1393
01:09:00,788 --> 01:09:01,721
and a back toss.

1394
01:09:02,088 --> 01:09:03,021
Spike.

1395
01:09:03,555 --> 01:09:04,955
- Spike.
- Out!

1396
01:09:04,955 --> 01:09:07,321
It's out.

1397
01:09:07,855 --> 01:09:12,355
Just like in their previous game,

1398
01:09:12,355 --> 01:09:16,155
Wonder Dogs players look
a bit stiff and tense.

1399
01:09:16,155 --> 01:09:17,255
(Wonder Dogs gave up two points.)

1400
01:09:20,155 --> 01:09:21,121
Relax.

1401
01:09:22,888 --> 01:09:24,121
The score is 2 to 0.

1402
01:09:24,888 --> 01:09:26,855
(Serve ace Ui Jeong again!)

1403
01:09:35,621 --> 01:09:37,221
(An unstable reception)

1404
01:09:37,221 --> 01:09:38,088
Jin.
Go in!

1405
01:09:38,988 --> 01:09:40,821
(Shaky toss)

1406
01:09:41,921 --> 01:09:43,555
To the left.

1407
01:09:43,555 --> 01:09:44,855
Their defense starts shaking.

1408
01:09:46,421 --> 01:09:48,721
(An attack connected from a quick toss)

1409
01:09:48,721 --> 01:09:50,355
Chae Yeon aims at the middle.

1410
01:09:50,355 --> 01:09:52,121
It's saved.

1411
01:09:52,488 --> 01:09:53,688
The ball is out.

1412
01:09:54,588 --> 01:09:57,921
(Ha Kyung drove the team
to three consecutive points.)

1413
01:09:57,921 --> 01:09:59,355
- Sorry.
- No, it's okay.

1414
01:10:01,021 --> 01:10:02,955
Unlike in the previous game,

1415
01:10:02,955 --> 01:10:06,221
they're facing professional players,
who follow patterned plays,

1416
01:10:06,221 --> 01:10:08,588
so they need to prepare a bit faster.

1417
01:10:11,888 --> 01:10:13,655
Enkhsoyol, is the ball too low?

1418
01:10:14,355 --> 01:10:16,455
Set the ball higher.

1419
01:10:17,488 --> 01:10:19,288
They're just nervous now.

1420
01:10:20,721 --> 01:10:22,688
- Isn't Jin the most nervous one?
- Yes.

1421
01:10:23,555 --> 01:10:25,021
The setter is off right now.

1422
01:10:25,021 --> 01:10:29,888
Jin is losing confidence in her sets,

1423
01:10:29,888 --> 01:10:31,855
so the attack rhythm isn't stable.

1424
01:10:31,855 --> 01:10:35,988
Basically, the setter's sets aren't
very smooth.

1425
01:10:36,455 --> 01:10:38,588
She needs to shake off the nerves quickly.

1426
01:10:40,121 --> 01:10:41,555
The score is 3 to 0.

1427
01:10:41,555 --> 01:10:42,855
(Ui Jeong's third consecutive serves)

1428
01:10:44,988 --> 01:10:45,921
Jin!

1429
01:10:46,455 --> 01:10:47,388
Jin.

1430
01:10:47,621 --> 01:10:49,721
(The toss dropped way too low
under the net.)

1431
01:10:55,055 --> 01:10:56,088
Jin.

1432
01:10:56,088 --> 01:10:57,321
They weren't in sync.

1433
01:10:58,488 --> 01:11:00,588
(The ball is handed over
to the opposing team's setter.)

1434
01:11:01,488 --> 01:11:03,388
(A back toss this time)

1435
01:11:05,821 --> 01:11:06,655
Spike!

1436
01:11:06,655 --> 01:11:08,455
(Powerful spike)

1437
01:11:10,855 --> 01:11:12,655
- Nice!
- Su Min scored a point.

1438
01:11:12,655 --> 01:11:17,355
The Altos players are running
the game with ease.

1439
01:11:17,688 --> 01:11:21,855
Even so, it was a ball
the Wonder Dogs should be able to handle,

1440
01:11:21,855 --> 01:11:23,721
- but they were too rushed.
- Right.

1441
01:11:33,921 --> 01:11:34,855
Jin!

1442
01:11:34,855 --> 01:11:36,455
Where did I tell you to position yourself
for defense?

1443
01:11:36,721 --> 01:11:38,788
You should mark the right side!

1444
01:11:42,288 --> 01:11:44,688
(Ho Chul is excited.)

1445
01:11:45,121 --> 01:11:47,121
With a score of 4 to 0,
the Altos are in the lead.

1446
01:11:49,455 --> 01:11:50,888
(Unstable reception)

1447
01:11:50,888 --> 01:11:51,855
The reception was too short.
Go!

1448
01:11:54,255 --> 01:11:56,555
(Will their attack work this time?)

1449
01:11:58,088 --> 01:11:58,988
Spike.

1450
01:11:59,221 --> 01:12:00,655
- It's out.
- They made an error.

1451
01:12:00,655 --> 01:12:04,088
The Altos are scoring easily,

1452
01:12:04,088 --> 01:12:07,388
thanks to the Wonder Dogs'
unforced errors.

1453
01:12:08,288 --> 01:12:11,221
Should we call a timeout?

1454
01:12:14,555 --> 01:12:17,321
(Wonder Dogs' timeout)

1455
01:12:18,055 --> 01:12:21,421
What's wrong with you guys?

1456
01:12:21,421 --> 01:12:23,355
Did I tell you to go deeper in
for the reception?

1457
01:12:23,355 --> 01:12:25,788
- No.
- Right. I told you to focus on attacking.

1458
01:12:25,788 --> 01:12:27,055
- I told you, right?
- Yes.

1459
01:12:27,721 --> 01:12:30,021
(Coach Kim's winning strategy
against the Altos)

1460
01:12:30,855 --> 01:12:33,421
(Hit relentlessly against low blocks.)

1461
01:12:34,288 --> 01:12:37,388
(Enkhsoyol kept attacking consecutively
even against low blocks.)

1462
01:12:37,721 --> 01:12:39,155
If that player receives,

1463
01:12:39,155 --> 01:12:41,455
- you go back and support.
- Okay.

1464
01:12:41,455 --> 01:12:43,321
- Then, it's your turn to attack.
- Okay.

1465
01:12:43,321 --> 01:12:45,388
- Where did I tell you to hit the ball?
- Hit it deep.

1466
01:12:45,388 --> 01:12:49,421
- Go out and hit it to the far side.
- Okay.

1467
01:12:49,421 --> 01:12:51,121
- Where should you cover in defense?
- The right side.

1468
01:12:51,121 --> 01:12:52,988
If the right side is open,
you go and cover it!

1469
01:12:52,988 --> 01:12:54,888
These are all the instructions
I gave already.

1470
01:12:54,888 --> 01:12:56,855
You're making too many early mistakes.

1471
01:12:56,855 --> 01:13:00,188
We decided not to make
mistakes at the start.

1472
01:13:00,188 --> 01:13:02,055
- What's wrong with you?
- Let's start over.

1473
01:13:02,055 --> 01:13:06,255
Ha Kyung did well sending
it to the right. Look.

1474
01:13:06,688 --> 01:13:10,088
Watch whether the middle blocker is
moving or not,

1475
01:13:10,088 --> 01:13:12,121
stay relaxed, and time the quick attack...

1476
01:13:12,121 --> 01:13:14,221
- before giving the ball.
- Okay!

1477
01:13:15,255 --> 01:13:17,721
(Don't reveal the direction of your toss.)

1478
01:13:18,055 --> 01:13:19,288
- Let's try it this way.
- Okay!

1479
01:13:19,288 --> 01:13:20,221
- Okay?
- Understood!

1480
01:13:20,655 --> 01:13:22,105
The first ball worked well so far,
so keep it up.

1481
01:13:22,788 --> 01:13:24,055
- Let's go!
- Go!

1482
01:13:25,321 --> 01:13:26,521
Relax.

1483
01:13:29,221 --> 01:13:31,521
(The Wonder Dogs' timeout is over.)

1484
01:13:32,155 --> 01:13:34,221
(Reminding the players
of the attack strategies)

1485
01:13:35,488 --> 01:13:37,288
Enkhsoyol, you just handle
the balls coming forward.

1486
01:13:37,288 --> 01:13:38,388
Do not dodge.

1487
01:13:38,388 --> 01:13:39,855
If you'll catch it, don't miss it.

1488
01:13:40,188 --> 01:13:41,588
Now, we need to score.

1489
01:13:43,021 --> 01:13:44,921
(Wonder Dogs desperately need
even a single point.)

1490
01:13:45,488 --> 01:13:47,888
The score is already stretched out
to 5 to 0 in the early stages.

1491
01:13:49,721 --> 01:13:51,588
Hey.

1492
01:13:51,588 --> 01:13:53,655
Enkhsoyol's reception is shaky.

1493
01:13:55,088 --> 01:13:56,555
(You know what to do against low blocks.)

1494
01:13:57,388 --> 01:13:58,488
Enkhsoyol!

1495
01:14:00,188 --> 01:14:01,288
They barely managed to send the ball over.

1496
01:14:01,288 --> 01:14:02,921
Ha Kyung sets the ball.

1497
01:14:03,755 --> 01:14:05,021
(A perfect set)

1498
01:14:07,288 --> 01:14:08,455
Min Kyoung!

1499
01:14:08,455 --> 01:14:09,455
Attack succeeds.

1500
01:14:10,921 --> 01:14:12,255
Hit it!

1501
01:14:12,255 --> 01:14:13,421
It was my mistake.

1502
01:14:19,388 --> 01:14:20,288
Song Hee.

1503
01:14:22,388 --> 01:14:23,655
Switch her with Enkhsoyol.

1504
01:14:24,921 --> 01:14:25,988
- Who?
- Enkhsoyol.

1505
01:14:25,988 --> 01:14:27,421
Enkhsoyol.

1506
01:14:27,421 --> 01:14:29,055
- Number three.
- Three?

1507
01:14:29,321 --> 01:14:31,188
Way to go!

1508
01:14:31,188 --> 01:14:32,021
Enkhsoyol is out,

1509
01:14:32,045 --> 01:14:34,745
and Han Song Hee is
in for her first match...

1510
01:14:34,746 --> 01:14:36,046
- with the Wonder Dogs.
- To your position.

1511
01:14:37,088 --> 01:14:38,988
Was the block high?

1512
01:14:38,988 --> 01:14:40,321
- No.
- Then, why did you try a feint?

1513
01:14:42,388 --> 01:14:43,221
Why did you try a feint?

1514
01:14:43,221 --> 01:14:44,555
- It was too short.
- What?

1515
01:14:44,555 --> 01:14:46,155
What does that have to do with it?

1516
01:14:46,155 --> 01:14:47,188
There was no block.

1517
01:14:47,188 --> 01:14:48,521
- You should've hit it instead.
- Okay.

1518
01:14:48,521 --> 01:14:49,988
If you keep this up, just quit the team.

1519
01:14:51,155 --> 01:14:52,755
I was very disappointed.

1520
01:14:52,755 --> 01:14:57,155
I'm not sure if it was
because she was too nervous,

1521
01:14:57,788 --> 01:15:00,388
but I don't want "she was nervous..."

1522
01:15:00,921 --> 01:15:05,742
used as an excuse for her performance.

1523
01:15:06,121 --> 01:15:12,288
That's usually the easiest excuse
for players.

1524
01:15:12,288 --> 01:15:15,455
I don't think her mindset...

1525
01:15:16,188 --> 01:15:19,555
in preparing for the match was proper.

1526
01:15:19,555 --> 01:15:20,955
I just can't understand...

1527
01:15:20,955 --> 01:15:27,755
those careless plays
and irresponsible attacks...

1528
01:15:27,755 --> 01:15:29,721
right from the start.

1529
01:15:33,021 --> 01:15:34,788
If you're going to play
without confidence,

1530
01:15:34,788 --> 01:15:35,821
- don't bother going in.
- Okay.

1531
01:15:35,821 --> 01:15:37,321
Just stay on the bench today.

1532
01:15:40,088 --> 01:15:41,855
When you go back in, play with confidence.

1533
01:15:45,521 --> 01:15:47,655
For now, watch and think
about how you should play.

1534
01:15:47,655 --> 01:15:48,955
The first ball came,

1535
01:15:48,955 --> 01:15:51,321
- and you just tipped it. Is that right?
- No.

1536
01:15:51,321 --> 01:15:54,721
If that's how you're going to play,
don't expect to step on the court again.

1537
01:16:00,221 --> 01:16:03,621
The Wonder Dogs haven't scored
any points yet.

1538
01:16:05,421 --> 01:16:07,688
(They need to turn the momentum around.)

1539
01:16:13,155 --> 01:16:15,188
An immediate point from Ha Kyung's spike!

1540
01:16:15,188 --> 01:16:17,621
It's an unexpected start
for the Wonder Dogs.

1541
01:16:18,121 --> 01:16:19,855
(Seven points earned in a row,
seven points lost in a row)

1542
01:16:21,113 --> 01:16:26,380
(It's not easy to close the score gap
against a pro team.)

1543
01:16:28,621 --> 01:16:30,321
Wonder Dogs need to get on the scoreboard.

1544
01:16:34,821 --> 01:16:35,788
Smash it!
Powerful strike!

1545
01:16:37,888 --> 01:16:39,988
(Following the strategy,
they hit a powerful spike.)

1546
01:16:40,221 --> 01:16:41,455
The back row is covering.

1547
01:16:41,821 --> 01:16:42,788
Min Kyoung.

1548
01:16:43,755 --> 01:16:45,088
(The Altos' counterattack)

1549
01:16:47,355 --> 01:16:48,588
(Another defense failure)

1550
01:16:48,588 --> 01:16:49,488
Spike!

1551
01:16:50,821 --> 01:16:53,721
Too many unforced errors are coming
in the early stages.

1552
01:17:00,247 --> 01:17:04,347
With a score of 8 to 0,
they reach the first technical timeout.

1553
01:17:05,055 --> 01:17:08,321
"At this rate,
our team may really fall apart."

1554
01:17:08,621 --> 01:17:12,355
Even if we lose, I'd be fine...

1555
01:17:12,355 --> 01:17:14,155
if we tried something,

1556
01:17:14,155 --> 01:17:18,688
but with so many unforced errors
from our side,

1557
01:17:19,055 --> 01:17:20,088
it was frustrating.

1558
01:17:20,088 --> 01:17:22,788
Down 8 to 0,

1559
01:17:22,788 --> 01:17:24,921
I kept thinking
about what I should do next...

1560
01:17:25,394 --> 01:17:28,894
as the team's coach.

1561
01:17:29,688 --> 01:17:31,487
(Technical timeout, 8:0)

1562
01:17:31,488 --> 01:17:33,316
It's the first technical timeout.

1563
01:17:34,203 --> 01:17:36,103
What's your problem?

1564
01:17:36,737 --> 01:17:37,837
What's going on?

1565
01:17:38,670 --> 01:17:39,770
It's all our mistakes.

1566
01:17:39,770 --> 01:17:41,170
- You couldn't even receive properly.
- Yes, Coach.

1567
01:17:41,170 --> 01:17:43,570
- They didn't do anything, did they?
- You're right.

1568
01:17:43,570 --> 01:17:44,937
What's wrong with you?

1569
01:17:44,937 --> 01:17:46,603
It's all our errors.

1570
01:17:46,603 --> 01:17:48,903
- It's eight to zero.
- Yes.

1571
01:17:50,937 --> 01:17:54,070
They have to move in a certain direction,

1572
01:17:54,070 --> 01:17:56,003
or select an empty spot to attack...

1573
01:17:56,003 --> 01:17:58,237
as they have planned before.

1574
01:17:58,237 --> 01:18:02,837
However, they couldn't even perform
basic skills at all.

1575
01:18:02,837 --> 01:18:06,003
Head coaches become speechless
at this point.

1576
01:18:08,303 --> 01:18:10,170
Jin, your back toss is a bit high.

1577
01:18:10,170 --> 01:18:12,737
You can make it faster.

1578
01:18:12,970 --> 01:18:15,803
(Starting from feedback on the setter)

1579
01:18:16,737 --> 01:18:19,570
I told you as we trained, Ha Kyung.

1580
01:18:20,103 --> 01:18:21,937
The ball will rise when it's hit.

1581
01:18:21,937 --> 01:18:25,570
So you must run to toss it
for the hitter to easily attack.

1582
01:18:25,570 --> 01:18:26,937
- Pass the ball properly.
- Understood.

1583
01:18:26,937 --> 01:18:27,970
- That's all you need to do.
- Yes.

1584
01:18:27,970 --> 01:18:29,370
- Okay?
- Yes.

1585
01:18:30,837 --> 01:18:32,603
Let's go!

1586
01:18:32,603 --> 01:18:34,737
(We'll keep this up in the first set.)

1587
01:18:37,303 --> 01:18:39,570
The setter has to hold the team together.

1588
01:18:39,570 --> 01:18:40,870
I like the sign.

1589
01:18:40,870 --> 01:18:42,637
Su Min, was my toss a little weak?

1590
01:18:42,637 --> 01:18:44,070
I'll go stronger.

1591
01:18:44,603 --> 01:18:47,203
(The opposing team finishes
adjusting their aim.)

1592
01:18:48,337 --> 01:18:49,403
It's eight to zero.

1593
01:18:49,403 --> 01:18:50,970
Wonder Dogs need their first point.

1594
01:18:51,670 --> 01:18:52,770
Serve!

1595
01:18:55,570 --> 01:18:58,370
(The Wonder Dogs haven't scored yet.)

1596
01:19:02,603 --> 01:19:03,737
She receives it.

1597
01:19:03,970 --> 01:19:06,237
(Jin, the setter, tosses it back.)

1598
01:19:07,670 --> 01:19:09,603
Their attack worked!

1599
01:19:09,603 --> 01:19:13,170
They managed to get their first point.

1600
01:19:13,170 --> 01:19:17,570
(They finally score.)

1601
01:19:21,437 --> 01:19:22,670
Nice!

1602
01:19:22,670 --> 01:19:24,937
Jin, toss the ball further.

1603
01:19:24,937 --> 01:19:25,937
Nice!

1604
01:19:27,203 --> 01:19:30,137
The Wonder Dogs score for the first time
after a technical timeout.

1605
01:19:30,137 --> 01:19:31,537
(Time to turn the tide)

1606
01:19:31,537 --> 01:19:32,570
Yoon Young In serves.

1607
01:19:35,670 --> 01:19:37,403
(The ball goes to the setter.)

1608
01:19:38,337 --> 01:19:40,303
(A setter tip)

1609
01:19:41,803 --> 01:19:43,737
(No block)

1610
01:19:44,537 --> 01:19:45,570
Kim Ha Kyung.

1611
01:19:46,003 --> 01:19:47,937
A powerful spike to the right!

1612
01:19:48,470 --> 01:19:50,803
- It's out.
- The ball went straight outside.

1613
01:19:51,537 --> 01:19:53,803
They're still many points apart,

1614
01:19:53,803 --> 01:19:55,403
but they're relaxed.
The game begins now.

1615
01:19:55,403 --> 01:19:56,403
You're right.

1616
01:19:58,503 --> 01:20:01,470
(Yoon Young In serves.)

1617
01:20:08,170 --> 01:20:09,170
Hwang Min Kyoung.

1618
01:20:10,737 --> 01:20:12,637
They receive it, and Lee Jin sets up.

1619
01:20:13,637 --> 01:20:14,870
(Our target is...)

1620
01:20:15,303 --> 01:20:18,337
(the left side with low blocks!)

1621
01:20:24,903 --> 01:20:26,537
Spike!

1622
01:20:27,370 --> 01:20:29,937
(Their strategy finally worked.)

1623
01:20:29,937 --> 01:20:31,103
Nice defense.

1624
01:20:31,103 --> 01:20:32,237
(Smiling)

1625
01:20:32,237 --> 01:20:34,603
Great job!

1626
01:20:35,237 --> 01:20:39,737
See how they hit the ball, Enkhsoyol?

1627
01:20:40,603 --> 01:20:42,537
- You saw the attack?
- I did.

1628
01:20:47,903 --> 01:20:51,370
(Altos 9 : Wonder Dogs 3)

1629
01:20:55,303 --> 01:20:58,137
Lee Jin uses a jump toss.

1630
01:20:59,703 --> 01:21:01,970
(But the toss is too low!)

1631
01:21:03,037 --> 01:21:04,337
They block, and it bounces off.

1632
01:21:05,703 --> 01:21:06,870
It goes to Hwang Min Kyoung.

1633
01:21:06,870 --> 01:21:08,003
(Hwang Min Kyoung attacks again.)

1634
01:21:08,770 --> 01:21:09,937
It hits the net!

1635
01:21:09,937 --> 01:21:11,203
(The ball hit the net, fortunately.)

1636
01:21:11,203 --> 01:21:12,870
- Sorry.
- No, it's okay.

1637
01:21:13,137 --> 01:21:14,203
We did it.

1638
01:21:14,203 --> 01:21:16,103
(Their block is tight. Toss higher!)

1639
01:21:16,337 --> 01:21:17,503
Jin!

1640
01:21:17,503 --> 01:21:19,403
Don't hit the edge of the ball.

1641
01:21:19,403 --> 01:21:21,470
- How can you attack with that?
- Understood.

1642
01:21:22,570 --> 01:21:26,937
The setter must be composed
for the Wonder Dogs to be stable.

1643
01:21:28,037 --> 01:21:29,070
Han Song Hee.

1644
01:21:32,770 --> 01:21:36,070
Hwang Min Kyoung's spike.

1645
01:21:36,370 --> 01:21:37,403
It's out!

1646
01:21:37,403 --> 01:21:39,037
- The ball is out.
- It's out of the court.

1647
01:21:41,703 --> 01:21:45,037
- The Altos are starting to make errors.
- Of course.

1648
01:21:45,037 --> 01:21:50,637
The Wonder Dogs must use that opportunity
to build their momentum.

1649
01:21:50,903 --> 01:21:53,070
They reduced the gap
from eight points to four.

1650
01:21:59,803 --> 01:22:00,837
It's a serving mistake.

1651
01:22:00,837 --> 01:22:03,203
(A serving error)

1652
01:22:04,003 --> 01:22:05,003
Attacking right away!

1653
01:22:05,003 --> 01:22:06,548
(Tumbling down)

1654
01:22:07,903 --> 01:22:11,070
(They fail to receive.)

1655
01:22:13,970 --> 01:22:15,237
Back attack from the right!

1656
01:22:15,237 --> 01:22:16,337
It's out.

1657
01:22:17,203 --> 01:22:18,270
Sorry, Jin.

1658
01:22:21,737 --> 01:22:22,737
Tamira!

1659
01:22:24,137 --> 01:22:27,637
They end up switching players
from Yoon Young In to Tamira.

1660
01:22:28,770 --> 01:22:32,037
Yoon Young In and Lee Jin are not in sync.

1661
01:22:32,037 --> 01:22:33,770
(Feeling sorry)

1662
01:22:34,337 --> 01:22:36,970
(Altos 12 : Wonder Dogs 6)

1663
01:22:38,203 --> 01:22:40,070
(Kim Na Hee serves.)

1664
01:22:40,437 --> 01:22:41,570
Hwang Min Kyoung.

1665
01:22:41,570 --> 01:22:42,570
Kim Ha Kyung.

1666
01:22:42,570 --> 01:22:44,570
- They pass the ball and block it!
- What a nice block.

1667
01:22:44,570 --> 01:22:46,203
The ball goes over
to Hwang Min Kyoung again.

1668
01:22:47,070 --> 01:22:48,370
Tamira receives it right away.

1669
01:22:48,370 --> 01:22:49,837
And Lee Jin uses a jump toss.

1670
01:22:54,670 --> 01:22:58,103
(The toss is low again!)

1671
01:22:59,470 --> 01:23:01,403
It manages to go over the net.

1672
01:23:03,203 --> 01:23:04,270
Hwang Min Kyoung!

1673
01:23:04,270 --> 01:23:05,437
(Hwang Min Kyoung spikes.)

1674
01:23:06,470 --> 01:23:07,503
(They lose a point.)

1675
01:23:07,522 --> 01:23:09,056
Her spike broke through the block.

1676
01:23:10,403 --> 01:23:16,303
I can see Lee Jin, the setter, is not
in her best condition.

1677
01:23:16,303 --> 01:23:18,770
Even though their set is not perfect,

1678
01:23:18,770 --> 01:23:21,770
a setter must deliver the ball first
for the hitter to attack.

1679
01:23:23,237 --> 01:23:25,570
Wonder Dogs give away the point again.

1680
01:23:28,503 --> 01:23:29,503
Na-Yeon, get in.

1681
01:23:33,203 --> 01:23:34,870
They change the setter.

1682
01:23:34,870 --> 01:23:37,803
The Wonder Dogs switch players often
in the first set.

1683
01:23:38,137 --> 01:23:39,803
Jin, which zone are you in?

1684
01:23:40,270 --> 01:23:41,503
Here. The last one.

1685
01:23:44,037 --> 01:23:45,170
I'm sorry.

1686
01:23:45,170 --> 01:23:51,070
No one can hit when you toss like that!
We had a chance.

1687
01:23:56,903 --> 01:23:59,303
Sorry, Jin. It's my mistake.

1688
01:23:59,770 --> 01:24:01,570
It's my fault. Sorry.

1689
01:24:04,403 --> 01:24:05,803
Come on.

1690
01:24:11,303 --> 01:24:12,903
Nice catch!

1691
01:24:15,837 --> 01:24:20,003
(Lee Jin's father)

1692
01:24:22,770 --> 01:24:24,203
I was in the starting lineup.

1693
01:24:24,203 --> 01:24:25,737
I shouldn't have done that.

1694
01:24:32,937 --> 01:24:34,103
I was a setter,

1695
01:24:34,737 --> 01:24:35,970
but I couldn't toss at all.

1696
01:24:37,103 --> 01:24:39,170
I think I got ahead of myself.

1697
01:24:39,170 --> 01:24:41,237
(Regret and disappointment flood in.)

1698
01:24:43,337 --> 01:24:45,637
I kept thinking, "Why did I do that?"

1699
01:24:53,070 --> 01:24:54,770
Outside the court,

1700
01:24:55,637 --> 01:24:59,603
I only thought of doing better
by watching Na-Yeon.

1701
01:25:02,103 --> 01:25:04,537
There are also short serves.
Watch carefully.

1702
01:25:05,770 --> 01:25:08,270
Na-Yeon, take it easy when you toss.

1703
01:25:08,270 --> 01:25:09,270
(Got it!)

1704
01:25:09,437 --> 01:25:12,470
(It's already their third substitution.)

1705
01:25:13,003 --> 01:25:14,170
(They have nowhere else to go.)

1706
01:25:14,170 --> 01:25:15,870
Look out for short serves!

1707
01:25:15,870 --> 01:25:17,103
Let's go!

1708
01:25:23,737 --> 01:25:25,170
(Nice reception)

1709
01:25:25,703 --> 01:25:28,970
Lee Na-Yeon sets up.

1710
01:25:29,937 --> 01:25:31,437
(Attack the left.)

1711
01:25:31,437 --> 01:25:33,303
(Mercilessly!)

1712
01:25:34,937 --> 01:25:36,103
Spike!

1713
01:25:41,370 --> 01:25:43,270
Nice one, Na-Yeon!

1714
01:25:48,737 --> 01:25:49,737
We all look down.

1715
01:25:49,737 --> 01:25:52,270
- Try to bring some energy.
- Okay.

1716
01:25:52,270 --> 01:25:53,937
Looking good!

1717
01:25:53,937 --> 01:25:56,403
They received the ball perfectly.

1718
01:25:56,403 --> 01:26:00,203
So it was important
for Lee Na-Yeon's first toss to go well.

1719
01:26:00,203 --> 01:26:02,870
- It sure is.
- Her toss was great.

1720
01:26:04,070 --> 01:26:06,803
(Altos 15 : Wonder Dogs 7)

1721
01:26:06,803 --> 01:26:07,803
Serve!

1722
01:26:12,603 --> 01:26:13,703
(Receiving smoothly)

1723
01:26:15,003 --> 01:26:16,603
(Targeting the left side again)

1724
01:26:18,037 --> 01:26:19,603
(Barely saving)

1725
01:26:20,570 --> 01:26:21,737
Go back!

1726
01:26:22,037 --> 01:26:24,970
Go Ui Jeong spikes.

1727
01:26:25,470 --> 01:26:28,337
Pass the ball!

1728
01:26:28,337 --> 01:26:30,003
(Going left with no doubt)

1729
01:26:30,003 --> 01:26:31,603
Nice!

1730
01:26:31,603 --> 01:26:32,837
(Pyo Seung Ju's spike)

1731
01:26:33,503 --> 01:26:34,537
A push shot!

1732
01:26:36,103 --> 01:26:37,103
They receive it.

1733
01:26:37,337 --> 01:26:38,337
Pyo Seung Ju attacks again.
It's weak!

1734
01:26:42,337 --> 01:26:45,003
A push shot, and they get a point!

1735
01:26:45,003 --> 01:26:46,837
(It wasn't weak at all?)

1736
01:26:46,837 --> 01:26:49,470
It's okay!

1737
01:26:49,470 --> 01:26:50,737
Ui Jeong.

1738
01:26:50,737 --> 01:26:53,603
You must hit the ball as you go up.

1739
01:26:53,603 --> 01:26:55,603
- That's how you get a point.
- Understood.

1740
01:26:56,603 --> 01:26:59,770
Hey, slow down.

1741
01:26:59,770 --> 01:27:01,070
(Tapping)

1742
01:27:02,570 --> 01:27:06,403
Pyo Seung Ju, who's a veteran player,

1743
01:27:06,403 --> 01:27:08,870
- is confidently leading the team.
- Right.

1744
01:27:09,470 --> 01:27:12,270
They're still many points apart,

1745
01:27:12,270 --> 01:27:15,503
but the mood can quickly change
with a small difference.

1746
01:27:15,503 --> 01:27:16,503
That's right.

1747
01:27:18,637 --> 01:27:19,837
Our serves are all facing front.

1748
01:27:19,837 --> 01:27:22,203
They all go to the opposite setter!

1749
01:27:22,203 --> 01:27:23,470
Our serves are all facing front.

1750
01:27:23,470 --> 01:27:25,970
They all go to the opposite setter!

1751
01:27:26,702 --> 01:27:30,536
(The previous serves kept going
to the center of the defense.)

1752
01:27:31,203 --> 01:27:32,270
Come on. Hit it in between.

1753
01:27:32,270 --> 01:27:33,403
Not straight down the middle.

1754
01:27:33,403 --> 01:27:34,836
Go for the gaps!

1755
01:27:34,836 --> 01:27:36,970
Song Hee, aim for the gaps!

1756
01:27:36,970 --> 01:27:37,970
I told you not to hit the middle.

1757
01:27:37,970 --> 01:27:39,303
Aim for the gaps.

1758
01:27:40,370 --> 01:27:42,903
(A tactic Coach Yeon Koung mentioned
from the video meetings)

1759
01:27:43,503 --> 01:27:45,770
(Hitting the serve in the gaps)

1760
01:27:47,070 --> 01:27:50,970
(If you serve the ball
right to the opponent's defense,)

1761
01:27:52,236 --> 01:27:56,270
(their setter can easily attack again
from her position.)

1762
01:27:57,603 --> 01:28:01,403
(However, if you hit the serve
in between them,)

1763
01:28:03,436 --> 01:28:07,070
(their pass can be off rhythm,)

1764
01:28:08,403 --> 01:28:12,903
(hence their setter's attack can be
off rhythm too.)

1765
01:28:13,303 --> 01:28:15,570
Let's make sure we hit the spot...

1766
01:28:15,570 --> 01:28:19,403
where the setter will have to go
behind the attack line.

1767
01:28:19,770 --> 01:28:20,870
If we can do that,

1768
01:28:21,736 --> 01:28:24,236
I'd say it's a successful serve.

1769
01:28:24,703 --> 01:28:26,803
Like Coach Yeon Koung said,

1770
01:28:27,203 --> 01:28:29,470
you have to make
the opposing setter run around...

1771
01:28:29,470 --> 01:28:32,770
and drain her energy
to win a volleyball game.

1772
01:28:32,770 --> 01:28:36,636
But the Altos' setter has been passing
very easily in her position,

1773
01:28:36,636 --> 01:28:38,670
- which means the serves were a bit weak.
- That's right.

1774
01:28:39,103 --> 01:28:40,303
Get on with the serve.

1775
01:28:40,303 --> 01:28:42,103
Hit it between them in the gaps.

1776
01:28:42,603 --> 01:28:45,203
(Got it, coach.)

1777
01:28:52,770 --> 01:28:54,203
(In between their defense)

1778
01:28:54,903 --> 01:28:55,870
(That's it!)

1779
01:28:56,236 --> 01:28:57,170
The defense is shaking.

1780
01:28:58,170 --> 01:28:59,203
Shoved it right through!

1781
01:29:08,603 --> 01:29:10,170
Nice!

1782
01:29:11,036 --> 01:29:12,003
Finally.

1783
01:29:12,736 --> 01:29:14,236
A successful serve at last.

1784
01:29:15,336 --> 01:29:18,303
(It's only the beginning now.)

1785
01:29:18,936 --> 01:29:21,770
If you see a line that seems weak,

1786
01:29:21,770 --> 01:29:23,370
you need to keep targeting it.

1787
01:29:23,370 --> 01:29:24,303
That's right.

1788
01:29:25,236 --> 01:29:26,570
One point at a time.

1789
01:29:27,570 --> 01:29:29,870
- You can't close a six-point gap at once.
- Of course not.

1790
01:29:33,903 --> 01:29:36,070
(The pass is short!)

1791
01:29:36,070 --> 01:29:39,103
It's fine. I'll get it.

1792
01:29:39,403 --> 01:29:43,970
We hit it where the setter will
have to come behind the attack line.

1793
01:29:45,870 --> 01:29:47,503
A backward set, but shaky.

1794
01:29:47,503 --> 01:29:49,436
(A shaky rally)

1795
01:29:50,136 --> 01:29:51,236
