Pyo Seung Ju to serve.

2042
01:42:00,454 --> 01:42:03,621
My bad.

2043
01:42:04,234 --> 01:42:09,101
The players need to feel the weight
of every single unforced error.

2044
01:42:10,054 --> 01:42:12,088
(Go Ui Jeong's serve follows.)

2045
01:42:13,654 --> 01:42:14,721
Pyo Seung Ju.

2046
01:42:14,721 --> 01:42:15,521
Lee Na-Yeon.

2047
01:42:18,388 --> 01:42:19,188
A strong spike!

2048
01:42:19,188 --> 01:42:20,254
Choi Yeon Jin receives.

2049
01:42:24,821 --> 01:42:25,721
Hit it!

2050
01:42:25,721 --> 01:42:27,054
Another strong spike!

2051
01:42:28,988 --> 01:42:30,654
She manages to receive that ball.

2052
01:42:34,088 --> 01:42:34,954
A strong spike!

2053
01:42:34,954 --> 01:42:36,388
(Another strong spike from Jeon Su Min)

2054
01:42:37,454 --> 01:42:41,021
(Gu Hye In fails to defend.)

2055
01:42:41,621 --> 01:42:44,321
Jeon Su Min is showing off
her powerful attack again.

2056
01:42:44,321 --> 01:42:45,854
(Second set, Altos 3 : Wonder Dogs 1)

2057
01:42:45,854 --> 01:42:47,788
Nice one, Jeon Su Min!

2058
01:42:48,954 --> 01:42:50,896
(A two-point difference in an instant)

2059
01:42:50,921 --> 01:42:51,954
Ah, I could have gotten that.

2060
01:42:52,688 --> 01:42:54,821
The difference in defense
feels significant.

2061
01:42:54,821 --> 01:42:56,021
(This doesn't feel good.)

2062
01:42:59,088 --> 01:43:00,721
- Hit it!
- A good reception.

2063
01:43:03,121 --> 01:43:04,154
She hit it, but...

2064
01:43:04,154 --> 01:43:05,554
(Out?)

2065
01:43:05,754 --> 01:43:07,221
Touch!

2066
01:43:09,121 --> 01:43:09,988
Wasn't that a touch-out?

2067
01:43:11,988 --> 01:43:13,621
It's called out.

2068
01:43:14,554 --> 01:43:15,854
I think it was a touch.

2069
01:43:15,854 --> 01:43:16,988
(We can't give up this point.)

2070
01:43:17,888 --> 01:43:19,688
She's requesting a video review...

2071
01:43:21,188 --> 01:43:22,977
to see if there was a touch-out
by the blocker.

2072
01:43:23,721 --> 01:43:26,421
(No touch)

2073
01:43:26,888 --> 01:43:28,288
The video review results...

2074
01:43:28,288 --> 01:43:30,421
show no touch.

2075
01:43:31,554 --> 01:43:32,954
The score is 4-1, a 3-point difference.

2076
01:43:32,954 --> 01:43:35,654
(Another point for Altos)

2077
01:43:36,654 --> 01:43:39,221
(The Wonder Dogs haven't scored
since their first point.)

2078
01:43:41,254 --> 01:43:42,188
A smooth serve.

2079
01:43:45,121 --> 01:43:46,221
(And another failed receive)

2080
01:43:46,221 --> 01:43:47,321
Hye In!

2081
01:43:47,321 --> 01:43:49,054
I told you there would be a short serve!

2082
01:43:49,107 --> 01:43:50,941
I told you to look
for the short one first!

2083
01:43:51,521 --> 01:43:54,154
(Gu Hye In's mistakes are
particularly frequent.)

2084
01:43:54,354 --> 01:43:56,188
That's an unbelievable mistake!

2085
01:43:56,188 --> 01:43:57,821
- It should be a good pass.
- Yes.

2086
01:43:57,846 --> 01:44:00,246
It's okay, reset. One more.

2087
01:44:00,854 --> 01:44:02,554
Score is 5-1, a 4-point difference.

2088
01:44:02,788 --> 01:44:04,754
They can't let the gap get any bigger.

2089
01:44:05,288 --> 01:44:06,988
(The game continues.)

2090
01:44:09,021 --> 01:44:11,721
(But it's another point for Altos.)

2091
01:44:14,554 --> 01:44:15,888
A block!

2092
01:44:15,888 --> 01:44:18,888
(Altos' continuous scoring)

2093
01:44:24,588 --> 01:44:25,554
My bad.

2094
01:44:28,088 --> 01:44:29,154
What should we do?

2095
01:44:31,988 --> 01:44:33,988
Nothing's working,
what are we going to do?

2096
01:44:35,321 --> 01:44:36,854
Think fast, anything!

2097
01:44:36,879 --> 01:44:38,513
(The rookie coach gets flustered
by the ominous development.)

2098
01:44:40,154 --> 01:44:41,088
A strong spike!

2099
01:44:41,554 --> 01:44:42,621
It's a success!

2100
01:44:42,621 --> 01:44:44,854
(A hard-won point...)

2101
01:44:50,288 --> 01:44:52,221
(is immediately followed
by another mistake from Gu Hye In.)

2102
01:44:52,221 --> 01:44:53,688
Hye In!

2103
01:44:53,688 --> 01:44:55,288
(Second set, Altos 9 : Wonder Dogs 4)

2104
01:44:55,288 --> 01:44:56,254
My bad.

2105
01:44:56,621 --> 01:44:58,488
(Wonder Dogs are no match...)

2106
01:44:58,754 --> 01:45:00,388
(for Altos' powerful offense.)

2107
01:45:00,388 --> 01:45:01,254
My bad.

2108
01:45:03,488 --> 01:45:07,854
(Is there nothing they can do but watch?)

2109
01:45:16,654 --> 01:45:20,088
(The captain, Hwang Min Kyoung, serves.)

2110
01:45:21,888 --> 01:45:22,888
Come on!

2111
01:45:24,488 --> 01:45:26,288
(A difficult toss)

2112
01:45:26,621 --> 01:45:28,421
She tosses it high,
and a strong spike by Pyo Seung Ju!

2113
01:45:28,421 --> 01:45:29,454
A great trajectory.

2114
01:45:29,454 --> 01:45:31,821
(A fantastic hit,
a point from a strong spike)

2115
01:45:31,996 --> 01:45:34,096
This is not going to be easy.

2116
01:45:34,121 --> 01:45:36,588
In this situation, the attackers need
to show a little more effort...

2117
01:45:36,588 --> 01:45:38,088
and move an extra step.

2118
01:45:39,154 --> 01:45:42,088
If we want to get a point,
we have to fight for it.

2119
01:45:42,088 --> 01:45:44,721
But the other team is scoring so easily.

2120
01:45:44,721 --> 01:45:46,252
I think this is how volleyball always is,

2121
01:45:46,277 --> 01:45:50,088
winning and losing
because of small things like this.

2122
01:45:50,088 --> 01:45:53,654
I need to focus even more.

2123
01:45:56,188 --> 01:45:57,154
The receive is short.

2124
01:45:57,721 --> 01:46:00,021
Go Ui Jeong.

2125
01:46:01,388 --> 01:46:02,254
(Block and a bounce)
Hyeon Jeong!

2126
01:46:08,688 --> 01:46:10,554
(Give it to me!)

2127
01:46:11,454 --> 01:46:12,254
It's mine.

2128
01:46:13,463 --> 01:46:15,354
She lifts it up with quick steps. A spike!

2129
01:46:16,821 --> 01:46:18,421
A touch-out by the blocker.

2130
01:46:18,421 --> 01:46:20,788
Pyo Seung Ju is gaining momentum!

2131
01:46:20,788 --> 01:46:22,854
Setter, just focus on yours!

2132
01:46:22,854 --> 01:46:23,754
Okay.

2133
01:46:26,388 --> 01:46:27,354
Bring in Myoung-Hwa.

2134
01:46:31,363 --> 01:46:32,786
(Kim Hyeon Jeong out, Moon Myoung-Hwa in)

2135
01:46:32,811 --> 01:46:35,521
- Let's go.
- We got this!

2136
01:46:36,654 --> 01:46:39,321
- Coach Kim sets up a wall.
- She is.

2137
01:46:39,321 --> 01:46:40,954
Moon Myoung-Hwa is in.

2138
01:46:41,421 --> 01:46:44,854
Moon Myoung-Hwa recorded
three blocks in the last game.

2139
01:46:45,200 --> 01:46:46,759
Myoung-Hwa, watch this side first.

2140
01:46:46,784 --> 01:46:48,206
(The four-spot)

2141
01:46:50,721 --> 01:46:54,254
(The four-spot that Moon Myoung-Hwa
will protect)

2142
01:47:00,388 --> 01:47:03,163
(She protected the four-spot well!)

2143
01:47:03,188 --> 01:47:04,188
Save it!

2144
01:47:04,888 --> 01:47:05,721
Go Ui Jeong.

2145
01:47:06,821 --> 01:47:08,488
Kim Na Hee with a diving dig!

2146
01:47:08,593 --> 01:47:10,254
- Come on!
- Hit it!

2147
01:47:11,388 --> 01:47:12,421
And Pyo Seung Ju!

2148
01:47:14,021 --> 01:47:15,154
(It's in!)

2149
01:47:15,554 --> 01:47:18,021
(Second set, Altos 9 : Wonder Dogs 7)

2150
01:47:18,188 --> 01:47:19,088
That's it!

2151
01:47:19,954 --> 01:47:21,188
Nice!

2152
01:47:27,541 --> 01:47:29,374
(And a fierce rally follows.)

2153
01:47:29,374 --> 01:47:30,341
That was a good reception.

2154
01:47:31,907 --> 01:47:33,041
Seung Ju's smash succeeded!

2155
01:47:33,041 --> 01:47:34,207
(Good straight spike!)

2156
01:47:34,207 --> 01:47:36,874
(Thanks to the consecutive points
earned by the reliable captain Pyo)

2157
01:47:36,874 --> 01:47:39,241
(Second set, Altos 6 : Wonder Dogs 4)

2158
01:47:39,474 --> 01:47:40,907
I told you to guard this side.

2159
01:47:41,941 --> 01:47:43,741
As the second set moves
past the middle stages,

2160
01:47:43,741 --> 01:47:47,041
Wonder Dogs are starting
to build some momentum.

2161
01:47:48,007 --> 01:47:49,174
Na-Yeon!

2162
01:47:49,174 --> 01:47:50,774
Position four.

2163
01:47:54,507 --> 01:47:56,507
(Target zone of the serve)

2164
01:47:59,374 --> 01:48:01,274
(The serve by Na-Yeon, the serve warrior)

2165
01:48:01,274 --> 01:48:02,141
Na-Yeon.

2166
01:48:04,733 --> 01:48:07,366
(It hit the spot!)

2167
01:48:09,107 --> 01:48:10,107
It's a contested ball.

2168
01:48:10,641 --> 01:48:11,907
(Is the Wonder Dogs' wall rising?)

2169
01:48:13,374 --> 01:48:14,241
A push shot!

2170
01:48:14,907 --> 01:48:15,841
It succeed!

2171
01:48:16,641 --> 01:48:19,774
It's a result of an excellent serve.

2172
01:48:19,774 --> 01:48:20,941
Exactly.

2173
01:48:21,474 --> 01:48:23,641
Stay focused!

2174
01:48:25,507 --> 01:48:27,307
Na-Yeon, good!

2175
01:48:27,307 --> 01:48:29,141
(That was a nice serve!)

2176
01:48:29,574 --> 01:48:31,241
(During the previous timeout)

2177
01:48:31,241 --> 01:48:34,174
Don't target the libero
when delivering a serve.

2178
01:48:34,174 --> 01:48:35,174
Don't send it to Min Kyoung...

2179
01:48:35,174 --> 01:48:37,741
- but to Ui Jeong.
- Okay.

2180
01:48:38,541 --> 01:48:40,841
(The Altos' back number ten, Go Ui Jeong)

2181
01:48:41,141 --> 01:48:43,541
As I mentioned earlier,
if they keep pressuring the server,

2182
01:48:43,541 --> 01:48:47,474
Yeon Jin, the setter,
could also get shaken.

2183
01:48:48,274 --> 01:48:50,007
It's 10 to 9,
just a 1-point difference now.

2184
01:48:54,341 --> 01:48:56,641
(Her strategy worked perfectly.)

2185
01:48:59,907 --> 01:49:00,807
Yeon Jin.

2186
01:49:01,607 --> 01:49:03,307
A quick attack through the middle!

2187
01:49:03,307 --> 01:49:05,841
(A quick attack
through the middle scored.)

2188
01:49:08,207 --> 01:49:10,741
(Totally satisfied)

2189
01:49:11,641 --> 01:49:14,441
(Will the fairy of victory...)

2190
01:49:14,441 --> 01:49:16,807
(smile upon the Altos again?)

2191
01:49:16,941 --> 01:49:18,074
I'll serve!

2192
01:49:18,074 --> 01:49:19,774
(The setter Yeon Jin's serve)

2193
01:49:21,307 --> 01:49:22,674
(Saving with a good reception)

2194
01:49:22,841 --> 01:49:23,707
Na-Yeon.
More!

2195
01:49:25,374 --> 01:49:26,307
B-quick.

2196
01:49:27,141 --> 01:49:28,007
It's saved.

2197
01:49:29,407 --> 01:49:31,274
- Spike, but it got blocked.
- Good.

2198
01:49:32,507 --> 01:49:33,374
Back to their court.

2199
01:49:34,241 --> 01:49:35,241
Mine!

2200
01:49:37,207 --> 01:49:39,341
(Error on the second-tempo play)

2201
01:49:40,741 --> 01:49:41,841
(Piercing glance)

2202
01:49:43,007 --> 01:49:44,041
A composed approach is needed.

2203
01:49:44,041 --> 01:49:45,274
Young In's back-to-back plays.

2204
01:49:45,274 --> 01:49:46,707
The ball comes right to MK!

2205
01:49:46,707 --> 01:49:48,274
She touched the net!

2206
01:49:48,274 --> 01:49:49,474
(Her body touched the net.)

2207
01:49:50,107 --> 01:49:52,874
They score on a net touch!

2208
01:49:53,174 --> 01:49:54,341
I'm sorry!

2209
01:49:54,341 --> 01:49:58,841
Hye In, "sorry" won't make it right!

2210
01:49:59,174 --> 01:50:00,074
Hey!

2211
01:50:00,074 --> 01:50:02,041
If you make a mistake again,
you'll lose this match!

2212
01:50:02,041 --> 01:50:03,874
- Lift it up!
- Okay!

2213
01:50:04,541 --> 01:50:05,407
I'm sorry.

2214
01:50:05,407 --> 01:50:08,074
Don't do anything to apologize for,
or you'll make the team lose.

2215
01:50:10,207 --> 01:50:11,041
"Sorry?" What the...

2216
01:50:14,041 --> 01:50:17,241
- We practiced it yesterday, right?
- Yes.

2217
01:50:24,507 --> 01:50:26,107
You're a bit out of it today.

2218
01:50:27,174 --> 01:50:29,841
You can do it, Hye In.

2219
01:50:30,674 --> 01:50:32,641
I think my performance today
was totally poor.

2220
01:50:32,641 --> 01:50:34,241
I messed up the second-tempo connections,

2221
01:50:35,274 --> 01:50:36,307
I couldn't receive properly,

2222
01:50:37,774 --> 01:50:39,507
and I couldn't hold my defensive ground.

2223
01:50:39,507 --> 01:50:41,607
(She showed shaky plays
throughout the game.)

2224
01:50:41,607 --> 01:50:43,074
I was rushing so much...

2225
01:50:43,641 --> 01:50:45,241
that I just did whatever I could.

2226
01:50:45,941 --> 01:50:47,274
Since it was a match against Altos,

2227
01:50:48,574 --> 01:50:52,907
I really wanted to show
how much I've improved,

2228
01:50:56,007 --> 01:50:58,107
but I couldn't show anything,

2229
01:50:58,107 --> 01:51:00,374
and I'm so frustrated with myself.

2230
01:51:03,141 --> 01:51:05,874
(Her desire to do better than anyone else
just got in the way,)

2231
01:51:05,874 --> 01:51:08,091
(and today's game didn't go well at all.)

2232
01:51:08,092 --> 01:51:10,027
It's okay to stay focus. Put it together.

2233
01:51:10,941 --> 01:51:12,741
(And her former teammate
in the warmup zone)

2234
01:51:13,374 --> 01:51:15,374
I've only been making mistakes
on the court.

2235
01:51:15,374 --> 01:51:16,841
No. You did well.

2236
01:51:17,674 --> 01:51:19,307
You can go back in anytime.

2237
01:51:25,507 --> 01:51:28,874
(They spent a lot of time together
before the match.)

2238
01:51:30,341 --> 01:51:33,241
Still, if we win this match,

2239
01:51:33,241 --> 01:51:35,774
- you know, it's going to feel amazing.
- It will feel really good.

2240
01:51:35,774 --> 01:51:37,174
We won't be happier.

2241
01:51:37,974 --> 01:51:40,541
(Quietly analyzing
the opposing team's performance...)

2242
01:51:40,541 --> 01:51:43,374
(and working on fitness together,)

2243
01:51:43,374 --> 01:51:45,974
(they prepared for this game
harder than anyone.)

2244
01:51:46,507 --> 01:51:48,641
(Although she's on the bench now,)

2245
01:51:49,474 --> 01:51:51,441
I hope our team wins the game,

2246
01:51:51,441 --> 01:51:54,741
and Su Bin does a good job
in her position.

2247
01:51:56,141 --> 01:51:58,207
(They're not running on the court
with the teammates,)

2248
01:51:59,174 --> 01:52:01,774
(but volleyball is like an orchestra,)

2249
01:52:03,041 --> 01:52:05,174
(so ordinary individuals come together...)

2250
01:52:05,174 --> 01:52:07,074
(and become one on the court.)

2251
01:52:08,441 --> 01:52:11,641
(That's how a team becomes complete.)

2252
01:52:11,641 --> 01:52:12,674
In 3, 2, 1.

2253
01:52:12,674 --> 01:52:14,174
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

2254
01:52:15,007 --> 01:52:17,574
(Cheering is also a part of play.)

2255
01:52:20,074 --> 01:52:20,874
Seung Ju.

2256
01:52:21,241 --> 01:52:22,441
(Telling her to serve)

2257
01:52:24,774 --> 01:52:27,374
(The target is Ui Jeong this time too.)

2258
01:52:31,707 --> 01:52:33,341
(The serve by Seung Ju, our ace)

2259
01:52:36,007 --> 01:52:38,141
The serve hit its mark!

2260
01:52:39,774 --> 01:52:40,707
Good.

2261
01:52:43,441 --> 01:52:45,607
Myoung-Hwa!

2262
01:52:45,607 --> 01:52:47,141
Awesome!

2263
01:52:53,341 --> 01:52:57,474
(A dramatic equalizer)

2264
01:52:59,274 --> 01:53:01,707
Su Bin, watch out for the quick attack!

2265
01:53:07,641 --> 01:53:08,507
Yeon Jin.

2266
01:53:10,607 --> 01:53:12,074
They failed to get the ball over the net!

2267
01:53:13,574 --> 01:53:14,441
Hitting from the position!

2268
01:53:14,441 --> 01:53:15,674
That's it.

2269
01:53:15,941 --> 01:53:16,907
Hitting from the position!

2270
01:53:16,907 --> 01:53:18,774
Wonder Dogs blocked it.

2271
01:53:19,274 --> 01:53:20,674
Myoung-Hwa
on the opposite side is jumping!

2272
01:53:22,541 --> 01:53:23,941
(They missed it.)

2273
01:53:23,941 --> 01:53:27,707
- Their attack worked.
- Ui Jeong delivered a clean attack.

2274
01:53:29,207 --> 01:53:30,107
Timeout.

2275
01:53:38,174 --> 01:53:41,307
(The Altos' timeout)

2276
01:53:41,307 --> 01:53:43,174
Don't panic.

2277
01:53:44,407 --> 01:53:46,507
From the tosses and the receiving...

2278
01:53:46,507 --> 01:53:47,807
to blocking,

2279
01:53:47,807 --> 01:53:49,074
nothing is executed properly.

2280
01:53:49,074 --> 01:53:52,141
One or two mistakes can lead
to consecutive points for the opponent.

2281
01:53:52,141 --> 01:53:53,674
That's not what we want. Be precise.

2282
01:53:53,674 --> 01:53:55,074
When the game isn't going well,

2283
01:53:55,074 --> 01:53:57,741
focus on doing everything accurately.

2284
01:53:57,741 --> 01:54:00,107
Not fast, but accurate.

2285
01:54:00,107 --> 01:54:01,274
- Got it?
- Yes.

2286
01:54:01,274 --> 01:54:03,507
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

2287
01:54:04,874 --> 01:54:06,774
- Focus.
- Okay.

2288
01:54:06,774 --> 01:54:09,574
The coach's outburst is starting
to show little by little.

2289
01:54:09,907 --> 01:54:12,941
He also gave a lot of instructions
to Setter Yeon Jin.

2290
01:54:13,974 --> 01:54:14,874
Yeon Jin,

2291
01:54:15,441 --> 01:54:17,207
- don't stand by in advance.
- Okay!

2292
01:54:20,341 --> 01:54:21,274
What's important is...

2293
01:54:21,274 --> 01:54:26,307
that Wonder Dogs started
to shift the momentum in their favor.

2294
01:54:26,941 --> 01:54:28,041
Go in, Chae-Rim.

2295
01:54:28,874 --> 01:54:29,841
Song Hee.

2296
01:54:29,841 --> 01:54:31,307
(Song Hee to Chae-Rim)

2297
01:54:31,307 --> 01:54:32,874
Good luck!

2298
01:54:33,974 --> 01:54:36,474
Hit it with intention.

2299
01:54:36,474 --> 01:54:38,007
(On the right side of the first row
of the Altos,)

2300
01:54:38,541 --> 01:54:40,974
(there's Su Min with low blocks.)

2301
01:54:41,507 --> 01:54:44,274
(The setter will set the ball,)

2302
01:54:44,274 --> 01:54:47,907
(and the hitter will aim her spike
at her fiercely.)

2303
01:54:47,907 --> 01:54:48,941
Let's go!

2304
01:54:48,941 --> 01:54:50,241
It's a serve by Ui Jeong.

2305
01:54:51,774 --> 01:54:53,874
The score is 12 to 11, a 1-point gap.

2306
01:54:53,874 --> 01:54:55,224
(Stop there, Wonder Dogs!)

2307
01:54:59,907 --> 01:55:03,407
(A merciless toss)

2308
01:55:04,474 --> 01:55:07,041
- Spike!
- That was a clean hit.

2309
01:55:07,041 --> 01:55:08,041
(This is the fierce spike!)

2310
01:55:10,707 --> 01:55:11,607
Sorry.

2311
01:55:14,641 --> 01:55:18,141
The reception was accurate
but slightly over,

2312
01:55:18,141 --> 01:55:20,607
yet the Na-Yeon player handled it well.

2313
01:55:20,607 --> 01:55:21,741
Since the ball was short,

2314
01:55:21,741 --> 01:55:24,374
she chased it quickly and made the attack.

2315
01:55:24,674 --> 01:55:26,107
This is what true team coordination
looks like.

2316
01:55:27,107 --> 01:55:29,374
Myoung-Hwa, do the same as before.

2317
01:55:30,374 --> 01:55:34,341
(A serve by Myoung-Hwa,
the wall of Wonder Dogs)

2318
01:55:37,149 --> 01:55:39,342
(They're clearly shaken.)

2319
01:55:41,307 --> 01:55:42,174
Tip it.

2320
01:55:44,307 --> 01:55:45,174
It goes over the net.

2321
01:55:46,574 --> 01:55:48,141
They touched the net!

2322
01:55:48,141 --> 01:55:50,007
(She touched the net slightly
with her hand.)

2323
01:55:51,007 --> 01:55:53,374
(Point awarded for a net touch)

2324
01:55:55,041 --> 01:55:56,274
Great!

2325
01:55:56,274 --> 01:55:59,007
In the last match,
Myoung-Hwa scored four points,

2326
01:55:59,007 --> 01:56:01,509
three from blocks and one from a serve.

2327
01:56:01,541 --> 01:56:05,707
And her serve worked well again.

2328
01:56:10,641 --> 01:56:13,174
(Myoung-Hwa was struggling with serves
throughout the training.)

2329
01:56:14,007 --> 01:56:15,974
Myoung-Hwa, let's go home!

2330
01:56:16,807 --> 01:56:21,907
(The painfully long serve training...)

2331
01:56:22,641 --> 01:56:26,007
(even made her cry.)

2332
01:56:29,974 --> 01:56:31,041
Myoung-Hwa is crying.

2333
01:56:33,982 --> 01:56:37,216
(The sorrow of the rookie can't...)

2334
01:56:37,241 --> 01:56:40,607
(be hidden by the blanket.)

2335
01:56:41,341 --> 01:56:43,541
You'll improve day by day.

2336
01:56:44,707 --> 01:56:45,774
Don't worry.

2337
01:56:45,774 --> 01:56:47,807
You're getting faster.

2338
01:56:48,441 --> 01:56:50,241
This is how you're going
to break your limit.

2339
01:56:50,241 --> 01:56:51,574
It'll happen.

2340
01:56:52,374 --> 01:56:53,507
Don't you worry.

2341
01:56:57,074 --> 01:56:58,974
The score is 13 to 12.

2342
01:56:58,974 --> 01:57:00,941
Wonder Dogs turned the tables around.

2343
01:57:01,507 --> 01:57:03,774
This is Wonder Dogs' first lead
in today's game.

2344
01:57:03,774 --> 01:57:04,741
Yes, the first lead.

2345
01:57:06,307 --> 01:57:09,141
(In total concentration)

2346
01:57:10,907 --> 01:57:11,974
She launches a serve.

2347
01:57:17,842 --> 01:57:18,855
She launches a serve.

2348
01:57:19,541 --> 01:57:20,541
(They're shaken.)

2349
01:57:20,541 --> 01:57:21,741
It's a nice serve.

2350
01:57:22,374 --> 01:57:23,441
What?

2351
01:57:23,441 --> 01:57:24,307
(Will it happen?)

2352
01:57:30,914 --> 01:57:34,148
(Rise, Queen of Serves!)

2353
01:57:34,148 --> 01:57:35,248
Moon Myoung-Hwa! Today's masterpiece!

2354
01:57:36,514 --> 01:57:37,448
Yes!

2355
01:57:41,414 --> 01:57:45,148
- Moon Myoung-Hwa is surely improving.
- Yes, she is.

2356
01:57:47,948 --> 01:57:49,481
Seriously, why are you doing so well?

2357
01:57:52,322 --> 01:57:54,556
Before Moon Myoung-Hwa came in,

2358
01:57:54,556 --> 01:57:56,889
the game felt like a thriller movie.

2359
01:57:56,889 --> 01:57:59,222
But now it's a romance.

2360
01:58:00,122 --> 01:58:02,952
(The thriller movie
from just 10 minutes ago)

2361
01:58:02,977 --> 01:58:04,865
Keep apologizing, and you lose the game!

2362
01:58:04,892 --> 01:58:06,698
- I said to raise it high!
- Okay.

2363
01:58:08,589 --> 01:58:10,856
(After a storm of shouting,)

2364
01:58:12,456 --> 01:58:14,922
(she is now speaking in a romantic voice.)

2365
01:58:16,489 --> 01:58:18,656
(What's wrong with our Myeong Hwa?
Why is she doing so well?)

2366
01:58:21,022 --> 01:58:24,622
Isn't my serve okay
even without a lot of speed?

2367
01:58:27,422 --> 01:58:28,522
I'm so proud of her.

2368
01:58:28,856 --> 01:58:34,289
As a coach, I'm so proud
when the players do well.

2369
01:58:34,656 --> 01:58:36,456
So, Moon Myoung-Hwa came in...

2370
01:58:36,456 --> 01:58:39,089
- And she's changing the mood.
- She completely changed it.

2371
01:58:50,422 --> 01:58:53,089
Coach Kim Ho Cheol is putting
in Kim Ha Kyung and Lee So Young.

2372
01:58:53,089 --> 01:58:55,047
That means he's getting desperate.

2373
01:58:58,589 --> 01:58:59,722
It's okay.

2374
01:59:00,556 --> 01:59:02,256
This might be a little difficult for us.

2375
01:59:03,756 --> 01:59:07,689
(The strongest players from Altos appear.)

2376
01:59:09,789 --> 01:59:10,756
It's okay.

2377
01:59:11,289 --> 01:59:15,489
(The battle of the coaches continues.)

2378
01:59:15,490 --> 01:59:17,490
(And the next match is...)

2379
01:59:17,731 --> 01:59:19,198
(Korea vs. Japan.)

2380
01:59:19,804 --> 01:59:20,863
(The world's strongest)

2381
01:59:21,109 --> 01:59:22,350
(A volleyball powerhouse)

2382
01:59:27,338 --> 01:59:28,805
(Facing a real-life "Haikyuu!")

2383
01:59:29,438 --> 01:59:31,638
(The opponent is the national champion
high school team.)

2384
01:59:32,205 --> 01:59:34,438
(They live and die for volleyball.)

2385
01:59:35,038 --> 01:59:37,638
(True volleyball fanatics)

2386
01:59:37,811 --> 01:59:39,578
(Expected score)

2387
01:59:39,772 --> 01:59:40,905
(3 to 0)

2388
01:59:40,905 --> 01:59:44,538
With my experience,
don't you think I'd be a better coach?

2389
01:59:44,538 --> 01:59:46,005
(The rookie coach's international debut.)

2390
01:59:48,273 --> 01:59:50,699
(The Wonder Coach)
